window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-021", "name_zh": "内在感官", "name_en": "Inner Senses", "tagline": "意识本有的第二套感官：不必经过五官，直接感知尚未变成物质的内在实相——人人都有，也可以练到清醒时使用。", "explanation": "内在感官是直接体验基本实在的感知能力，与外在感官不同，它们不依赖时空伪装模式。外在感官将能量转化为物质世界的伪装，而内在感官直接感知伪装之下的生命力与真实。内在感官持续运作，即便意识层面未察觉，没有它们，任何存在都不可能。它们能超越时空，因为时空本身就是伪装。内在感官如同连接不同场域的桥梁，将来自内在世界的活力数据传递给心智，再通过潜意识与大脑沟通。它们不扭曲现实，而是直接浸入价值气候的海洋，看穿伪装的变化。通过训练，可以有意识地使用内在感官，感知到分子舞蹈等未被外在感官扭曲的真实。内在感官本身即是行动，改变感知者与被感知者。它们与心理时间紧密相关，是通往更完整实相的关键。", "definitions": [{"zh": "内在感官处理的是实际存在的东西。", "en": "The inner senses deal with what actually is.", "source": "Session 19"}, {"zh": "内在感官关注的是伪装之下的生命力。", "en": "The inner senses are concerned with vitalities beneath the camouflage.", "source": "Session 19"}, {"zh": "内在感官是这两个场域之间的连接器之一。", "en": "The inner senses are one of the connectives between these two fields.", "source": "Session 25"}, {"zh": "内在感官被设计来让你感知内在实相。", "en": "The inner senses are equipped to let you perceive inner reality.", "source": "Session 37"}, {"zh": "内在感官以外在感官所不能的方式，对身体拥有直接、持续的知识。", "en": "The inner senses have an immediate, constant knowledge of the body in a way that the outer senses do not.", "source": "Session 20"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "内在感官是什么", "note": "赛斯第一次抛出这个词，定义给得极短：「感官之内的感官」¹——本也可以说成「感官背后的感官」，但他相信那样说会让人误解¹。同一节里分工也划了出来：你们一般的感官感知——用珍的说法，创造——一个外在世界，而在它们之内的感官，则感知并创造一个内在世界²。\n\n判断随之而来：这不是外加的超能力，而是意识的固有配备——「内在感官是意识的一个属性」³。意识具有内在的感官，这是所有的意识与生俱有的，不论它发展的程度如何，而且这些内在感官与某一意识采用肉体这种特殊形式、以便在某一系统内运作时所用的感官互不相涉⁴；每个读者到某个程度都经常在使用它们，只是在自我的层面上并不知道⁵。「所有的人格都有内在感官」，经由这些内在感官，通讯得以维持⁶——也正因为每个人都具有内在感官、不管自己是否知道这件事，这些感官都应该加以开发⁷。\n\n归属也一并交代清楚：内在感官属于人类人格未被物质显现的那部分，组织囊就是那个灵体的本质⁸；最基本的意识永远不是物质的，经验在物质世界汇集之后要由内我或星光本体编织成型，所以人类人格的真正本质，要看非物质自己与物质之间的连结、和其中运作的沟通系统⁹。\n\n最吃重的一句是：内在感官是为感知非实质资料而准备的，不被你投射入三次元实相的影像所欺骗，你的肉体感官是这些内在感知方法的延伸——死后你就得依赖它们，出体的经验中用到的也是它们，而它们继续不断地在醒时的意识之下运作¹⁰。把话说实：内在感官代表你真正的感知力量，是你本有的非实质感知「设备」，的确有你看不见的光、听不见的声音以及感觉不到的觉受，它们都属于内在感官的领域¹¹。最后留一句提醒：这些与肉体感官大致相应的内在感官，不必被训练去朝向一个特定的时空取向¹²。", "src": "第 14、202、297、359、515、522、539、793、900 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0001", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第14节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0002", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第14节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0387", "label": "早期课第7册 · 第297节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0415", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第515节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0416", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第515节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0426", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第522节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0394", "label": "早期课第8册 · 第359节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0344", "label": "早期课第5册 · 第202节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-021-e0347", "label": "早期课第5册 · 第202节"}, {"n": 10, "id": "q-concept-021-e0434", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第539节"}, {"n": 11, "id": "q-concept-021-e0474", "label": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第900节"}, {"n": 12, "id": "q-concept-021-e0467", "label": "心灵的本质 · 第793节"}], "groups": [{"label": "感官之内的感官", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0001", "zh": "透过感官产生美的感知，是你们层面上随后内在感知（inner perceptions）的触媒。以音乐为例，这两者是如此紧密相连，因此唯有透过这些感官，你们才能欣赏音乐。个体的心灵行动产生后，又引导个体超越感官。这里还有很多可以说的。我以后还会解释另一个名词——内在感官（inner senses）——你们会觉得非常有趣。我说的内在感官指的是，感官之内的感官。我也可以说是感官背后的感官，但我相信这样说会让人误解。", "en": "Perception of beauty through the senses is the trigger on your plane for subsequent inner perceptions. The two are so closely bound, through music for example, which can only be appreciated through the senses. Psychic actions take place which lead the individual beyond the senses. There is much more to be said here. There is a phrase which I will explain at a later date—inner senses—which you will find extremely interesting. By this I mean senses within the senses. I would use behind the senses but I believe this would lead to confusion.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第14节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "14", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0002", "zh": "在你们的层面上，一切事物都是某种东西的具体化，那个东西独立存在于你们层面之外。因此，在你们的感官之内，还有其他向内感知的感官。你们一般的感官感知——或像珍喜欢说的，创造——一个外在的世界。在它们之内的感官，也就是可辨识的感官之内的感官，感知并创造一个内在的世界。它们感知内在世界的一部分。我很难跟你们解释。无论如何，取决于你们居住的层面，你们一般的感官是受到限制的——就你们的状况来说，亲爱的朋友，在你们的层面上恐怕是极度受到限制的——所以，对应的内在感官也是受到限制的。", "en": "Everything on your plane is a materialization of something that exists independent of your plane. Therefore within your senses there are other senses that perceive inward. Your regular senses perceive, or as Jane would like to say create, an outer world. The senses within them, that is within the recognizable senses, perceive and create an inner world, they perceive part of an inner world. This is difficult for me to explain to you. However as your regular senses are limited according to the plane which you inhabit—in your case dear friends on your plane extremely limited, I’m afraid—so are the corresponding inner senses limited.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第14节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "14", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "意识的配备，人人都在用", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0387", "zh": "内在感官是意识的一个属性。外在感官使得这个资讯对物质有机体，以及身体意识、自我而言是有意义的。这是为了鲁柏的书。", "en": "The inner senses are an attribute of consciousness. The outer senses make this information meaningful to the physical organism, and the body consciousness, the ego. This is for Ruburt’s book.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第297节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "297", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0415", "zh": "现在：以一种非常真实的方式，你们所用的感官创造了你们所感知的环境（译注：佛家用语则为五根创造了五尘）。你们的肉体感官使得你们必然感知一个三次元的实相。可是，意识具有内在的感官。这是所有的意识与生俱有的，不论它发展的程度如何。这些内在感官与某一意识在采用某一特殊化的形式——譬如肉体——以便在某一特定系统内运作时所用的感官互不相涉。", "en": "Now: The senses that you use, in a very real manner, create the environment that you perceive. Your physical senses necessitate the perception of a three-dimensional reality. Consciousness is equipped with inner perceptors, however. These are inherent within all consciousness, regardless of its development. These perceptors operate quite independently from those that might be assumed when a given consciousness adopts a specialized form, such as a physical body, in order to operate in a particular system.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "515", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0426", "zh": "你可要明白，你那特定的一套伪装并非仅有的一套。其他的实相有完全不同的系统，但所有的人格都有内在感官，那是意识的属性，经由这些内在感官通讯得以维持，而正常的有意识自身对这些通讯很少知悉。我部分的目的就是让你们知道这些通讯中的一些。", "en": "Your particular set of camouflages is not the only set, you see. Other realities have entirely different systems, but all personalities have inner senses that are attributes of consciousness, and through these inner senses communications are maintained about which the normally conscious self knows little. Part of my purpose is to make some of these communications known.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第522节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "522", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0416", "zh": "因此，每个读者都有内在感官，并且到某个程度经常在使用它们。虽然在自我的层面上他并不知道他在这样做。至于我们，则相当自由且有意识地运用内在感官。果真你能这样做，那你便会知觉我生存于其内的那种环境。你会看到一个没有伪装的情况，在其内事件与形式是自由的，而非胶着在一个果冻似的时间模内。例如，你不仅能看见你目前的起居室好像聚集着一堆看来永恒的家具，而且你能够转移焦点，而看到组成各物的分子与其他粒子极广大而恒常的舞蹈。", "en": "Each reader, therefore, has inner senses, and to some extent uses them constantly, though he is not aware of doing so at an egotistical level. Now, we use the inner senses quite freely and consciously. If you were to do so, then you would perceive the same kind of environment in which I have my existence. You would see an uncamouflaged situation, in which events and form were free and not stuck in a jellylike mold of time. You could see, for example, your present living room not only as a conglomeration of permanent-appearing furniture, but switch your focus and see the immense and constant dance of molecules and other particles that compose the various objects.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "515", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0467", "zh": "你有与你的肉体感官大致相应的内在感官。不过，这些不必被训练去朝向一个特定的时空取向。", "en": "You have inner senses that roughly correlate with your physical ones. These, however, do not have to be trained to a particular space-time orientation.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第793节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "793", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0394", "zh": "朱莉、史蒂芬还有彼得——你们都应该阅读所有能找得到的超心理学和心灵现象书籍，你们读得越多，就越能了解彼得的能力，而且越能开发你们自己更多的能力。因为每个人都具有内在感官，不管自己是否知道这件事，这些内在感官都应该加以开发。", "en": "Julie, Steve, and Pete—You should all read any books you can find concerning parapsychology and psychic phenomena. The more you read the more you will understand of Pete's ability, and the more indeed that you can develop your own abilities. For each individual has inner senses, whether or not he knows that he does, and these should be developed.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第359节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "359", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "属于非物质自己，肉体感官是它的延伸", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0344", "zh": "如你们所知，内在感官是属于人类人格未被物质显现的那部分。在不同的时间，我曾经提过你们所谓灵体的实相，你们应该记得一年多前我们讨论过的组织囊，那就是灵体的本质。它是由电磁成分组成的，简单地说，它就是看不见的自己。", "en": "Now. As you know, the inner senses belong to that part of human personality that is not physically materialized. At various times I have spoken concerning the reality of what you refer to as the astral body. You must remember that over a year ago we discussed tissue capsules. The astral body is of this nature. It is composed of electromagnetic components. It is simply the unseen self.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第202节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "202", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0347", "zh": "最基本的意识永远不是物质的。但在你们的系统却必须透过身体系统，也就是肉体，汇集经验。但经验本身不是物质的，无法被物质所包含。因此这些在物质世界所汇集的经验，就会被内我或星光本体（astral identity）编织成型。只有了解物质和非物质自己之间的连结，和在其中运作的沟通系统，那么人类人格的真正本质才能被了解。 当我们谈到你们的族类时，你们必须明白，所有的意识都有它自己的星光本体。内在感官是这个非物质自己的一部分，它让人格保留了它和非物质实相的关系，也让物质取向的自己专注在地球的环境。", "en": "The basic consciousness is never physical. Yet within your system it must collect experience within the physical system, hence the physical body. But experience itself is not physical, and cannot be contained within physical matter. Therefore this experience, collected within the physical field, is held in codified form by this inner self or astral identity. It is only by understanding the connection between the physical and nonphysical self, and the communication systems that operate here, that the true nature of human personality can be studied. While we are dealing now with your own species, it should be realized that all consciousness also possesses its own astral identity. The inner senses are part of this nonphysical self. They allow the personality to retain its relationship with nonphysical reality, permitting the material self to focus within its earthly environment.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第202节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "202", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0434", "zh": "内在感官是为感知非实质资料而准备的，它们不被你投射入三次元实相的影像所欺骗。其实，它们也能感知实质的物体。你的肉体感官是这些内在感知方法的延伸，在死后你就得依赖它们了。你在“出体”的经验中用到了它们。它们继续不断的在醒时的意识之下运作。", "en": "The inner senses are equipped to perceive data that is not physical. They are not deceived by the images that you project in three-dimensional reality. Now, they can perceive physical objects. Your physical senses are extensions of these inner methods of perception, and after death it is upon these that you will rely. They are used in out-of-body experiences. They operate constantly beneath normal waking consciousness…", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第539节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "539", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0474", "zh": "举例来说，你所看见的那些画存在于那儿，而它们每一个方面都与你画室里的画一样真实。在这儿我并不是象征性的说。的确有你看不见的光，你听不见的声音，以及你感觉不到的觉受，所有这些都属于内在感官的领域。内在感官代表你真正的感知力量，它们代表了，好比说，你本有的非实质感知“设备”。你可以相当容易的分辨肉体感知：你可以分辨你看见的与你听见的东西，如果你闭上眼睛你就看不见了。", "en": "The paintings that you have envisioned, for example, exist there, and they are every bit as real as the paintings in your studio. I am not speaking symbolically here. There is indeed light that you do not see, sound that you do not hear, sensation that you do not feel. All of these belong to the realm of the inner senses. The inner senses represent your true powers of perception. They represent, say, your native nonphysical perceptive “equipment.” The physical senses are relatively easy to distinguish: You know what you see from what you hear. If you close your eyes, you do not see.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第900节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "900", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "内在感官与外在感官的分野", "note": "内在与外在之间「并没有实际的区隔」，分成两套只是为了方便讨论——表面的外在感官只和一个特定层面的特定伪装有关，内在感官则和伪装之下的生命力有关；他还给过一个比喻：内在感官像隐藏的地下火车，把重要的燃料从一个国家运送到另一个国家¹。分工写成两句对照：外在感官主要地、专门地处理伪装模式——据他所知，只处理伪装模式；内在感官处理伪装模式下面的实相，并把内在实相的资料运载到身体的感官²。方向与内容都不同的另一条是：内在感官从实相的内在世界传递资讯给身体，外在感官从伪装的外在世界传递资讯给身体，而内在感官一直在觉察身体自己的生理数据，对身体有着「直接又不变的认识」——这是外在感官没有的，它主要只关心身体与伪装环境的关系³。\n\n判准一句话：内在感官提供直接的经验，外在感官提供转译、扭曲过的伪装二手经验⁴。由此派生四点：① 五官会被自己的错觉骗——桌子不是固体，你们的科学家知道这一点，而当外在感官经验它为固体时，那是它们的错觉；内在感官「不会这样受骗，也从未受过骗」，它直接经验构成你们物质的实相⁵；② 层面限制不同——内在感官可以在所有层面上以及所有情况下运作，外在感官则按层面和情况变化，只在自己被建构出来的那一个层面上才值得信赖⁶；③ 认识内在实相只有一条路——只有透过内我以及内在感官才能直接认识内在实相，智力的任务本来就是应付和解读伪装存在的实相⁷；④ 眼镜的比喻——肉体感官自身即为伪装的一部分，它们好似覆盖在你们天生的内在感知上的眼镜，强迫你把一个可见的活动场「看」作实物，而人内在有些感知方法可以看透伪装的背景、看穿舞台，只是自己的演员部分太贯注于戏里而不察⁸。\n\n还要补上另一面，免得读成虚无：并不是说物质实相是假的，而是意识以各种装扮来表现它自己，实质的画面仅只是感知这些装扮的无数方法之一，内在感官却打开了你感知的范围，允许你以自由得多的方式去诠释经验、创造新的形式和新的通道⁹。切换的必要性也就写在了这里：那只是你们用肉体感官感知到的唯一实相，为了感知其他实相，你们必须从外在感官切换到内在感官——它比较清楚、有足够的能力感知行动和实相，且不必依赖肉体感官所造成的扭曲就可以存在¹⁰。纯度的定性句收尾：不受伪装资讯束缚的内在感官，或多或少是「纯粹」的感知器，在没有任何桎梏之下，对很多实相的感知几乎不带任何偏见¹¹。", "src": "第 19、20、31、33、37、95、154、162、515、522 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0014", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第19节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0027", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第20节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0030", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第20节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0119", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第33节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0173", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第37节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0113", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第31节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0307", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第95节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0422", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第522节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-021-e0418", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第515节"}, {"n": 10, "id": "q-concept-021-e0337", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第162节"}, {"n": 11, "id": "q-concept-021-e0335", "label": "早期课第4册 · 第154节"}], "groups": [{"label": "五官只看伪装，内在感官看伪装之下", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0014", "zh": "精神酵素是转化剂（transformers），而且我曾说过，它们非常重要。我谈到内在感官和外在感官，好让我们比较容易讨论。然而现在，你们一定知道内在和外在之间并没有实际的区隔。表面的外在感官，只和一个特定层面的特定伪装有关，内在感官和伪装之下的生命力有关。如果我可以再次用一个比喻来形容，这些内在感官就像隐藏的地下火车，把重要的燃料从一个国家运送到另一个国家。", "en": "Mental enzymes are the transformers, and as I have said they are extremely important. I have spoken of the inner and outer senses to make our discussion easier. However you must know by now that there is no actual distinction between inner and outer. The apparent outer senses are merely concerned with the particular camouflage of a particular plane. The inner senses are concerned with vitalities beneath the camouflage. These inner senses, if I may use an analogy again, are like hidden underground trains that carry important fuel from one country to another.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第19节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "19", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0027", "zh": "正如我所说的那样，外在感官，主要地、专门处理伪装模式，而且就我所知，它们只处理伪装模式。内在感官，我亲爱的约瑟，它处理伪装模式下面的实相，把这些实相，把这些内在实相的资料运载到身体的感官。因此，这些内在感官，在某种程度上，完全有能力以一种肉眼看不见的方式看到身体的内部。", "en": "As I have said, the outer senses deal mainly and as far as I know exclusively with camouflage pattern. The inner senses, my dear Joseph, are senses which deal with realities beneath camouflage patterns, and which carry data of these realities, these inner realities, to the body. These inner senses therefore are thoroughly capable of seeing the inside of the body, in a way that the outer eyes cannot.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0030", "zh": "内在感官从实相的内在世界传递资讯给身体。外在感官从伪装的外在世界传递资讯给身体。不过，内在感官一直在觉察身体自己的生理数据（physical data），而外在感官则主要关心身体与伪装环境的关系。换句话说，内在感官对身体有着直接又不变的认识，这是外在感官没有的。", "en": "The inner senses deliver data from the inner world of reality to the body. The outer senses deliver data from the outside world of camouflage to the body. However, the inner senses are aware of the body’s own physical data at all times, while the outer senses are concerned with the body mainly in its relationship to camouflage environment. In other words the inner senses have an immediate, constant knowledge of the body in a way that the outer senses do not.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0173", "zh": "约瑟，这恐怕是有点复习的味道，你们知道桌子不是固体。你们的科学家们知道这一点。当你们的外在感官经验它们为固体的时候，那是它们的错觉。但内在感官不会这样受骗，也从未受过骗。内在感官直接经验构成你们物质的实相。", "en": "The table, and I’m afraid this is somewhat review, Joseph, the table as you know is not solid. Your scientists know this. Your outer senses lie when they experience the table as solid. You know this. The inner senses are not so deceived, and never have been. The inner senses experience directly the reality of which your matter is composed.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0422", "zh": "在他内有些感知的方法可允许他看透伪装的背景，看穿舞台。他经常运用这些内在感官，虽然他自己的演员部分是如此地贯注于戏里而对此不察。以广义的方式来说，肉体感官实际上形成了它似乎唯一能感知的那个物质实相。它们自身即为伪装的一部分，但它们好似覆盖在你们天生的内在感知上的眼镜，强迫你把一个可见的活动场“看”作实物；因此你只能靠它们告诉你在表面上所发生的事。例如你能说出其他演员的位置或时钟的时间，但这些肉体感官却不会告诉你时间自身即为一个假相，或意识形成其他的演员，或你所看不见的实相存在于那真是如此明显的实物之外。", "en": "Within him there are methods of perception that allow him to see through the camouflage settings, to see beyond the stage. He uses these inner senses constantly, though the actor part of himself is so intent upon the play that this escapes him. In a large manner, the physical senses actually form the physical reality they seem to only perceive. They are themselves part of the camouflage, but they are like lenses over your natural inner perceptions that force you to “see” an available field of activity as physical matter; and so they can be relied upon only to tell you what is happening in a superficial manner. You can tell the position of the other actors for example, or time by clock, but these physical senses will not tell you that time is itself a camouflage, or that consciousness forms the other actors, or that realities that you cannot see exist over and beyond the physical matter that is so apparent.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第522节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "522", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0418", "zh": "并不是说物质实相是假的，而是说，意识以各种装扮来表现它自己，而实质的画面仅只是感知这些装扮的无数方法之一而已。肉体感官迫使你将经验转译为物质性的感知，而内在感官却打开了你感知的范围，允许你以自由得多的方式去诠释经验，而创造新的形式和新的通道，经由它，你任何的意识能认识自己。", "en": "It is not that physical reality is false. It is that the physical picture is simply one of an infinite number of ways of perceiving the various guises through which consciousness expresses itself. The physical senses force you to translate experience into physical perceptions. The inner senses open your range of perception, allow you to interpret experience in a far freer manner and to create new forms and new channels through which you, or any consciousness, can know itself.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "515", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "内在感官不扭曲，也不受层面限制", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0119", "zh": "有些时候，你们或许能够体验我的结构。你知道，内在感官提供直接的经验。外在感官则提供转译、扭曲过的伪装二手经验。", "en": "At some time you may be able to experience my structure. You see, the inner senses provide direct experience. The outer senses provide camouflaged distortions of translated second handed experience.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第33节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "33", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0113", "zh": "内在感官可以在所有层面上以及所有情况下运作。外在感官则会按照层面和情况而有所变化。外在感官只有在自己被建构出来的那一个层面上，才值得信赖。目的当然是让有意识的人格认得出来，就像伪装模式也只有在某些情况下才有效。", "en": "The inner senses operate on all planes and under all circumstances. The outer senses vary according to plane and circumstance. The outer senses are dependable only in terms of the definite plane for which they were constructed. Their purpose of course is to enable the conscious personality to recognize as valid camouflage patterns which are only valid under certain conditions.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第31节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "31", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0335", "zh": "不受伪装资讯束缚的内在感官，或多或少是纯粹的感知器，在没有任何桎梏之下，对很多实相的感知几乎不带任何偏见。", "en": "The inner senses, by being free of camouflage information, are more or less （in quotes） “pure” perceptors, perceiving with but little prejudice of many realities while being imprisoned by none.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第154节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "154", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0307", "zh": "再重复一次，我不是要贬低智力的重要性：只有透过内我，以及内在感官才能直接认识内在实相。智力必须要应付和解读伪装存在的实相，这就是它的目的。", "en": "It is not to minimize the importance of the intellect that I once again repeat: Inner reality will only be known directly through the inner self, and the inner senses. The intellect must deal and interpret the realities of camouflage existence, this being its purpose.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0337", "zh": "不过，这并不代表说这是唯一的实相，那只是你们用肉体感官感知到的唯一实相。为了感知其他实相，你们必须从你们的外在感官切换到内在感官，因为内在感官比较清楚，而且有足够的能力感知行动和实相，因为它不必依赖肉体感官所造成的扭曲就可以存在。", "en": "This does not, however, mean that this is the only reality. It is simply the only reality that you perceive with the physical senses. In order to perceive other realities, you must therefore switch from your outer senses to the inner senses, for the inner senses are clearer, and are equipped to perceive action and reality as it exists independently of the distortions given to it by the physical senses.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第162节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "162", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "它们如何运作", "note": "先钉住位置并给出警告：科学家知道大气对他们的仪器有一种扭曲效应，却不了解他们的仪器本身必然会造成扭曲——而有一种仪器比任何其他仪器都重要，它给了你们人类所有的突破和进步，那就是头脑，或者更确切地说是「包含头脑的心智」，它是内在感官与外在感官的交会处¹。接着把链条拆成清清楚楚的几步，冒着说再说的风险也要说清：内在感官把这个重要的资讯传送到心智，对身体与外在伪装模式接触而言是重要的任何原料则送给头脑，而「所谓潜意识，是心智和头脑、内在感官和外在感官之间的连结物」——它一部分在你们层面、一部分在其他层面，其较大的部分属于内在世界，当资讯从内在世界进入潜意识时，它能够深入内在世界本身²。心智这一头再补一句：心智接收这内在实相的资讯，没有伪装的心智是个接收台，这里你拥有的几乎是一个内在的神经通讯系统，与你们熟悉的外在系统非常相像³。\n\n换成转换器一说：各种各样的资料被送进人格之内的合适通道、绕过一般物质的通道，因此它们可以并肩存在，自己也得以穿越物质空间和时间旅行⁴。觉察是分级进行的：全我一直不断经验所有内在感官传来的资料，内在自我当然觉察到这一点，潜意识有时觉察，外在自我觉察得非常少——理由是外在自我必须把大部分能量集中用于生存和操控外在的伪装世界，而这个世界由内我创造，其持续存在由内我持续的警觉决定⁵。\n\n另有两条性质别漏。其一，感知本身就是行动：内在感官和行动的本质以及电磁实相都有关联，因为内在感官的感知本身即是行动，所以它们改变了知觉者和被知觉物本身⁶；据此，每个个体透过内在感官的运用、遵循某些已经提过的规则，创造了任何既定的物质实体⁷；外在实相是内在电磁实相的物质化、所有的经验都经过电磁编码，内在感官直接接收这个资料，而要在意识上觉察这样的资料、或要让肉体感官能够留下印象，就一定会出现某种翻译⁸。醒时的对照是：你在有意识的层次上对实质的资料反应——周围的噪声、尖锐的刹车声、汽车逼近的视觉震撼——而那景象或事件的整个内在事实，却即刻被你的内在感官「认知」；实质资料经由神经来传达时必然发生「时间消逝」，那代表感知光谱有时间性的那一端⁹。\n\n其二，结构位置：把全我想成存在于你们层面、由身体、意识自我与内我合成的场域单位，则存有场域与全我场域之间的这个连结——在你们的层面——就是内在感官¹⁰；也所以，你一直与自己的存有接触，因为心智本来就是存有的一部分，当前的人格和存有之间的沟通，是透过内在感官去执行的¹¹。", "src": "早期课第1册第 19、20、21、25、35 节；早期课第3册第 126、137 节；早期课第5册第 202 节；早期课第7册第 289 节；个人实相的本质第 625 节；早期课第2册第 67 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0023", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第19节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0032", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第20节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0031", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第20节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0320", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第126节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0146", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第35节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0351", "label": "早期课第5册 · 第202节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0329", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第137节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0381", "label": "早期课第7册 · 第289节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-021-e0445", "label": "个人实相的本质 · 第625节"}, {"n": 10, "id": "q-concept-021-e0090", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第25节"}, {"n": 11, "id": "q-concept-021-e0047", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第21节"}], "groups": [{"label": "内在通讯系统：心智、潜意识、头脑", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0023", "zh": "科学家知道地球的大气是一个扭曲，或者说对他们的仪器而言有一种扭曲效应。他们不了解的是，他们的仪器本身必然会造成扭曲。这件事再怎么强调都不为过。有一种仪器比任何其他任何仪器都重要，它给了你们，也就是人类，所有的突破和进步，那就是头脑。或者更确切地说，包含头脑的心智，它是内在感官与外在感官的交会处。", "en": "Scientists realize that the atmosphere of the earth is a distortion, or has a distorting effect upon their instruments. What they do not understand is that their instruments themselves are bound to be distortive. This cannot be emphasized too strongly. Any material physical instrument will have built-in distortive effects. The one instrument which is more important than any other and which has given you, that is mankind, all its breakthroughs and advance is the brain. Or rather the mind which contains the brain, and which is the meeting place of the inner and outer senses.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第19节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "19", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0031", "zh": "我说过，透过这些内在感官，资料（material）从内在世界被传递给身体。心智接收这内在实相的资讯。这一点非常重要。没有伪装的心智是个接收台，接收内在感官给它的资讯。这里你拥有的几乎是一个内在的神经通讯系统，与你熟悉的外在系统非常相像。", "en": "The material is delivered to the body, as I have said, from the inner world by means of these inner senses. This inner reality data is received by the mind. This is extremely important. The mind, being un-camouflaged, is the receiving station for the data brought to it by the inner senses. What you almost have here is an inner nervous and communication system closely resembling the outer systems with which you are familiar.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0032", "zh": "虽然冒着一说再说的风险，但我想要这些步骤清清楚楚。内在感官把这个重要的资讯传送到心智。对身体与外在伪装模式接触而言是重要的任何原料，则是送给头脑。所谓潜意识，是心智和头脑，内在感官和外在感官之间的连结物。它其实一部分在你们层面，一部分在其他层面。潜意识有些部分的确是和伪装模式、目前人格个人的过去、种族的伪装记忆打交道；它较大的部分则属于内在世界，当资讯从内在世界进入潜意识时，它能够深入内在世界本身。", "en": "I risk repeating myself, but I want these steps to be plain. This vital data is sent to the mind by the inner senses. Any material that is important for the body’s contact with outer camouflage patterns is given to the brain. The subconscious, so-called, is a connective between mind and brain, between the inner senses and the outer senses. It is actually partly on your plane and partly on other planes. Portions of it do deal with camouflage patterns, with the personal past of the present personality, with racial camouflage memories; and the greater portion belongs to the inner world, and as data comes into it from the inner world, so can it reach far into the inner world itself.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0320", "zh": "内在感官可以被想成是转换器，各种各样的资料被送进人格之内的合适通道，绕过一般物质通道的通道。因此它们可以并肩存在。基于各种我还没有给你们的原因，自己得以穿越物质空间和时间旅行。这些原因与内我的电子现实有关，也与存在于电子场域之内的肉身对等物有关。", "en": "The inner senses can be thought of as transformers, where various kinds of data is sent to proper channels within the personality, channels which bypass ordinary physical channels. They then can exist side by side. There are various reasons, which I have not yet given you, that allow for the traveling of the self through physical space and time. These reasons have to do with the electric actuality of the inner self, and with that counterpart of the physical body which exists within the electric field.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第126节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "126", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0146", "zh": "其实，全我一直不断经验所有内在感官传来的资料。内在自我当然觉察到这一点。潜意识有时觉察到这一点，而外在自我觉察到的非常少。其中的原因，我在过去的课程已经解释过了。外在自我必须将其大部分能量集中用于生存和操控外在的伪装世界。这个世界是由内我创造的，它的持续存在则是由于内我持续不断的警觉决定。", "en": "The fact is that the whole self is constantly experiencing data from all of the inner senses. The inner ego is of course aware of this. The subconscious is sometimes aware of this, and the outer ego is aware of very little. I have explained the reasons for this in past sessions. The outer ego must concentrate much of its energy toward survival in and manipulation of the outer camouflage world. This world has already been created by the inner self, and its continuing existence is determined by the constant vigilance of the inner self.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "感知本身就是行动", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0351", "zh": "现在。内在感官和行动的本质以及电磁实相都有关联，因为内在感官的感知本身即是行动，因为如此，它们改变了知觉者和被知觉物本身。你会发现，即使星光形象也总是在动，从来都不是静止，而它的状态改变了物质性的自己，即便物质的自己是跟着星光形象行动的。", "en": "Now. Regard the inner senses in connection with the nature of action and electromagnetic reality, for the perceptions of the inner senses are themselves action, and as such they change both the perceiver and the thing perceived. You can see then that even this astral image is always in motion and never static, and its condition alters the physical self even as the physical self acts upon the astral image.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第202节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "202", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0329", "zh": "今晚我们要来思索一下本体的本质。在我们稍早前就物质的本质所作的讨论中，我们清楚表明，每个个体透过内在感官的运用，遵循某些已经提过的规则，创造了任何既定的物质实体。", "en": "We will further consider this evening the nature of identities. In our earlier discussions concerning the nature of matter, we made it plain that each individual created any given material object, through use of the inner senses, and following certain rules which were mentioned.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第137节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "137", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0381", "zh": "我告诉过你，外在实相是内在电磁实相的物质化。我告诉过你，所有的经验都经过电磁编码。内在感官直接接收这个资料，你看，就像在上周五的事件那样。如果你在意识上觉察到这样的资料，或是要让肉体感官能够留下印象，就一定会出现某种翻译。", "en": "I have told you that exterior reality is a materialization of inner electromagnetic reality. I have told you that all experience is electromagnetically coded. The inner senses pick up this data directly, you see, as in last Friday’s episode. Some translation must occur if you are to become aware consciously of such material, or if it is to impress the physical senses at all.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第289节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "289", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0445", "zh": "在有意识的层次上，你对实质的资料反应，比如周围的噪声，也许是尖锐的刹车声、眼见汽车逼近的视觉震撼等，但是，那个景象或事件的整个内在事实，却即刻被我所谓的你的“内在感宫”（见此节尾的注）所“认知”。内在感官对我说过的那些“内在模式”反应。实质的资料经由神经来传达时，必然发生“时间消逝”。这代表了“感知的光谱”（spectrum of perception）有时间性的那一端。", "en": "Consciously you react to the physical data — the noise, the squeal of brakes perhaps, the visual shock of seeing the car so close, but the entire inner reality of that scene or event is instantly “recognized” by what I refer to as your inner senses. (See the note at the end of the session.) These respond to the interior patterns I’ve told you about. The physical data is carried through the nerves with the necessary time lapses that must occur. These represent the temporal end of the spectrum of perception.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第625节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "625", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0282", "zh": "在我离题之前，我正在切入的重点是，物质是被内在感官利用也被外在感官感知的行动。", "en": "The main point, before I get sidetracked, that I was building up to, is that matter is action utilized by the inner senses and perceived by the outer senses.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第67节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "67", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "存有与人格之间的连结", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0090", "zh": "如果你们为了简化而把全我想成（我希望），存在于你们的层面，带着它的身体、意识自我与内我三部分，合成一个场域单位，这个单位也是更大或更完整存有的一部分，就像一个场域单位在另一个场域单位之内，那么，也许你就不难想像，存有场域与全我场域之间的这个连结或连结之一，在你们的层面，这个连结就是内在感官——也就是说，内在感官是这两个场域之间的连结物之一。", "en": "If you will think （I hope） for simplicity’s sake of the whole self as it exists on your plane with its physical body, conscious ego and inner self as one field unit, which is also part of the larger or more complete entity as one field unit within another, then perhaps it will not be too much for you to imagine the connection, or one of the connections, between the entity field and the whole-self field, which is on your plane as being the inner senses—that is, the inner senses are one of the connectives between these two fields.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第25节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "25", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0047", "zh": "你有时很傻，约瑟。丢脸。你从前面我提供的讯息、以及上面的段落，你就应该知道，你一直与自己的存有接触，因为，首先心智本来就是存有的一部分。我已经告诉过你，当前的人格和存有之间的沟通，是透过内在感官去执行的，并且我也告诉过你，在这些课中你都有使用内在感官。所以，问题本身就是解答。", "en": "You are silly sometimes, Joseph. For shame. From the information you have been given before, and from the above paragraph, you should know that you are in contact with your own entities, in that the mind is a portion of the entity to begin with. I have told you that communication between a present personality and the entity is carried on by means of the inner senses, and I have told you that in these sessions you use the inner senses. Surely then the question answers itself.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第21节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "21", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "九种内在感官（上）：第一到第五", "note": "名单要先记住赛斯自己的免责声明，否则会把它当成分类学：这些内在感官是整体在运作，「它们之间的分类，是我为了简洁说明而有点武断制定的」¹；虽然过去他把机能与特性分开描写，它们其实一同运作，以你们的想法很难分开²。还留了一句常被略过的话：在「内我」惯用的感官之外另有潜伏的内在感官，有些无法以具体方式表达、只能用比喻暗示³。\n\n第一种是直接的触碰：你不仅可以看到如你所见的街道，或听到飘进你耳朵的些许声音，你其实也在一定范围内直接经验每件事物的本质——这种经验是即时的，包含的东西也比从外在感官接收到的一般资料还多⁴。罗的编注把它称作「内在振动性触觉」，并转述《灵界的讯息》第十九章的写法：站在街上的观察者会「变成」他注意范围内所选的任何东西——人们、树木、昆虫、草叶——同时保有自己的意识⁵。\n\n第二种被并入心理时间来介绍：所谓的心理时间属于内我、也就是心智，它是一个连结物，是一种内在感官的一部分，为了方便起见将称之为第二内在感官⁶；外在物理时间是一个完全的伪装，而心理时间是一条天然通道，作用是来回内在世界与外在世界的一条捷径——你们并没有这样利用它⁷。\n\n第三种处理过去、现在与未来的感知：它能让内在自我和存有经验直接的观念模式，因此让它们摆脱连续因果的限制⁸；实际限度也要补上——你们永远不会获得完全的即时认知，但可以偶尔不去理会时间的界限，至少隐约瞥见实相和观念⁹。\n\n第四种是观念感官：它又涉及对观念的直接认识，这种认识方式远超过你们所谓的理智方式¹⁰。最好用的例子是：假设你突然了解宇宙是一体的概念，用的就是这种内在感官——于是你建构梦意象时会造出种类繁多的形状和形式；你不会想着当一只鸟是什么感觉，你会有片刻就是一只鸟¹¹。\n\n第五种是「认识见多识广的本质」，它与第四种不同、不涉及对观念的认识¹²；判据是：如果没有任何第五种内在感官的使用，人类甚至就无法相互了解——你们的用语「设身处地」最贴近这个意思¹³。", "src": "早期课第1册第 20、23、34、36、37、38 节；梦、进化与价值完成第 900 节；灵魂永生第 581、583 节；早期课第6册第 268 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0186", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第38节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0475", "label": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第900节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0440", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第583节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0130", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第34节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0438", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第581节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0059", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第23节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0060", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第23节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0162", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第36节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-021-e0166", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第37节"}, {"n": 10, "id": "q-concept-021-e0175", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第37节"}, {"n": 11, "id": "q-concept-021-e0370", "label": "早期课第6册 · 第268节"}, {"n": 12, "id": "q-concept-021-e0187", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第38节"}, {"n": 13, "id": "q-concept-021-e0193", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第38节"}], "groups": [{"label": "编号只是讲解的权宜", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0186", "zh": "只有在这种情况下，戏剧提供了它自己的演员。再一次，请记得这些感官，这些内在感官是整体在运作，而且至少在某种程度内，它们之间的分类，是我为了简洁说明而有点武断制定的。", "en": "Only in this case the dramatization provides its own actors. I am going to leave further discussion of this sense until some later session, when after additional material you will be able to understand it more thoroughly. And again remember that these senses, these inner senses, operate as a whole, and that at least to some degree the divisions between them are somewhat arbitrary on my part, and are made for the sake of simplicity.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第38节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "38", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0475", "zh": "虽然我在过去曾借分开其机能与特性来描写内在感官，但基本上它们以这样一种方式一同运作，以致以你们的想法，会很难将一个与另一个分开。它们以一种完美的自发秩序作用，觉察到所有的同步性。那么，在那心理宇宙里，存有是可能“同时无所不在”，同时觉察到每件事的。你们的世界是由这种“存有”——那形成你身体的意识单位——所组成的。你有的那种意识心无法保有那种资讯。", "en": "The inner senses, though I have in the past described them by separating their functions and characteristics, basically operate together in such a way that in your terms it would be highly difficult to separate one from the others. They function with a perfect spontaneous order, aware of all synchronicities. In that psychological universe, then, it is possible for entities “to be everywhere at once,” aware of everything at once. Your world is composed of such “entities”—the units of consciousness that form your body. The kinds of conscious minds that you have cannot hold that kind of information.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第900节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "900", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0440", "zh": "因此之故，理论上你是可能由一只青蛙、或一只鸟、或一只蚂蚁的眼中看世界的。在此我们谈的是肉体的感官。在意识向一个特定的伪装系统对准频率时，“内我”通常所应用的感官之外，也有潜伏的“内在感官”。不过，有些内在感官是无法以具体方式来表达的，只有用比喻来暗示它们的性质。在本书中没有必要讨论它们。它们属于一本特为讨论内在的感知方法的书。", "en": "It is therefore theoretically possible for you to see the world through a frog’s eye, or a bird’s or an ant’s. We are speaking here of physical senses. The inner self has also latent inner senses beside the ones that it normally uses while the consciousness is tuned into a particular camouflage system. Some, however, are inexpressible in physical terms, and only analogies could be used to hint of their nature. In this book there is no need to discuss them. They belong in a book given more specifically to interior methods of perception.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第583节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "583", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "第一种 · 直接触碰本质（内在振动性触觉）", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0130", "zh": "这最后一点格外重要，我会很快回到这里再谈。打个非常简单的比喻好了，透过内在感官，你不仅可以看到如你所见的街道，或听到飘进你耳朵的些许声音。你其实也在一定范围内直接经验每件事物的本质。这种经验是即时的，而且，打个比喻，包含的东西也比从外在感官接收到的一般资料还多。也就是说，你不但可以闻到气味，而且是平常透过关着的窗户往外看时，你闻不到的，你还可以实际感觉到树木与树枝以及隐藏的鸟儿与昆虫其统一的本质。你直接经验到汽车里驾驶人员的人格——甚至汽车分子成分的生命力，并且在那个焦距内，“看见”（加引号）一切事物未来与过去的经验。这个范围本身大很多。", "en": "This last is extraordinarily important and I shall return to it shortly. Through the inner senses, and using a very simple analogy, you would not only see the street as you do or hear the few sounds that drift to your ears. You would actually experience directly the essence of everything within a certain range. This experience would be instantaneous and would, using the analogy, include more than the usual data that you would receive from the outer senses. That is, not only would you be able to feel the air though you were not out in it, not only would you pick up the odors, though ordinarily you cannot do this while you look out through closed windows, but you would literally feel the unitary essences of the trees and branches and hidden birds and insects. You would experience directly the personalities of the inhabitants of the automobiles—the vitality even of the components of the automobiles’ molecules, and “see” （in quotes） the future and the past experience of everything within that particular range of focus. And the range itself would be much larger.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第34节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "34", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0438", "zh": "（译注：由构成万物之EE单位发散出之“光”或“气”，克里安照相可显示。） （*罗注：“内在振动性触觉”是我们的“内在感官”之一。赛斯在《灵界的讯息》的第十九章列出了这些感官。改写于下：用这感官，一个站在一条典型的街上的观察者会有这样的经验：他会“变成”在他注意力范围内他所选择的任何东西：人们、树木、昆虫、草叶。他会保留他自己的意识，而多少以我们现在感觉冷热的方式去感知种种感觉。这感官像是“神入”或称“同理心”，但更生动得多。）", "en": "No. Inner vibrational touch is a much more personal experience, more like “becoming a part of” that which you perceive, rather than for example a reading of an aura. (Pause.)", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第581节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": "罗的编注 · 转述《灵界的讯息》第十九章", "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "581", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0040", "zh": "这是属于内在感官的性质之一。我会更深入地讨论它，你们可称这个为第一种内在感官。", "en": "This is one of the qualities belonging to the inner senses. I will go into it more deeply but you may call it the first inner sense.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "第二种 · 心理时间", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0059", "zh": "所谓的心理时间属于内我，也就是说属于心智。不过它是一个连结物，是一种内在感官的一部分，为了方便起见我们将称之为第二内在感官。", "en": "Psychological time so-called belongs to the inner self, that is to the mind. It is however a connective, a portion of one of the inner senses, which we will call for convenience the second inner sense.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0060", "zh": "外在物理时间是一个完全的伪装，在你们层面基本上并非必要；但你们让它变得好像非要不可，因为你们拒绝承认内我是整个人格的一部分，所以无法在你们层面上充分利用心理时间的优点。心理时间，就像我说过的，是一条天然通道，一种内在感官的一部分，作用是来回内在世界与外在世界的一条捷径。你们并没有这样利用它。", "en": "Outer physical time is a complete camouflage, unnecessary basically on your plane; but you have made it seem necessary because of your refusal to admit the inner self as part of your whole personality, and therefore you have not been able to utilize psychological time to its fullest advantage on your plane. Psychological time as I have said is a natural pathway, part of an inner sense, that was meant as an easy access from the inner to the outer world and back again. You do not use it as such.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "第三种 · 过去、现在与未来的感知", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0162", "zh": "在我们结束之前，我想提一下第三种内在感官对观念模式（concept patterns）经验的重要性。第三种内在感官，涉及你们称之为过去、现在和未来的感知，它能让内在自我和存有经验直接观念--模式，因此让它们摆脱连续的困果限制。", "en": "Before we close I want to mention the importance of the third inner sense with the experience of concept patterns. The third inner sense, involving what you would call perception of past, present and future, is the sense that enables the inner ego and entities to experience direct concept-patterns, and free them therefore from successive cause and effect limitations.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第36节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "36", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0166", "zh": "第三种内在感官，就像我已经告诉你们的，在一定程度上会使你们从过去、现在和将来的结构中释放出来，而且理论上也可以获得即时认知（instant cognition）。就实际情况来看，你们永远不会获得这样的即时认知，但将可以偶尔不去理会时间的界限，而至少可以隐约瞥见我所说的实相和观念。", "en": "The third inner sense, as I have told you, will enable you to some extent to free yourselves from the constructions of past, present and future, and will permit in theory instant cognition. As far as practice is concerned you will never achieve such instant cognition, but you will be able to set aside now and then the boundaries of time, and you will be able at least to glimmer the reality and the concepts of which I speak.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0163", "zh": "我想多说一点第三种内在感官与观念之间的关系。", "en": "I wanted to say more concerning the third inner sense in connection with concepts.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "第四种 · 观念感官", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0175", "zh": "第四种内在感官是一种观念感官（conceptual sense）。现在，你们是以意念（idea）的角度来思考观念（concept），而意念你只能用理智的方式理解。然而，第四种内在感官（注：观念的直接体验，涉及从原来的形式，转变为另一个形式）又涉及对观念的直接认识，这种认识方式远超过你们所谓的理智方式。", "en": "The fourth inner sense is the conceptual sense. Now you think of a concept in terms of an idea, which you can only understand in intellectual terms. However, the fourth inner sense involves again direct cognition, only now of a concept in much more than you would call intellectual terms; It involves experiencing a concept completely, to the extent of being a concept completely.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0370", "zh": "不过，我想要把这一点讲得更清楚。假设你突然了解宇宙是一体的概念，就要用到感觉概念的这一种内在感官，那么当你建构梦意象时，你就会建构种类繁多的形状和形式。以此代表生命的复杂多样。然后，你会有进入这些生命当中每一个的经验。你不会想着当一只鸟是什么感觉，你会有片刻就是一只鸟，这确实涉及各种投射，但还是必须称之为伪投射。", "en": "I want to make this clearer however. Suppose that you suddenly understand the concept of oneness with the universe, and that this particular inner sense of feeling concepts is to be used. You would then construct, as you construct dream images, a multitudinous variety of shapes and forms meant to represent the complicated varieties of life. You would then have the experience of entering into each of these lives. You would not think what it was like to be a bird, you would momentarily be a bird. This does involve a projection of sorts, and yet it still must be called a pseudo projection.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第268节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "268", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "第五种 · 认识活组织的本质", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0187", "zh": "第五种内在感官带着我们沿着这个方向往前进，而且也涉及我会称为认识见多识广的本质（cognition of the knowledgeable essence）。这种内在感官与第四种内在感官不同，它不涉及对观念的认识。", "en": "The fifth inner sense carries us further along in this direction, and involves what I will call cognition of the knowledgeable essence. This sense differs from the fourth inner sense in that it does not involve the cognition of a concept.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第38节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "38", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0193", "zh": "如果没有任何第五种内在感官的使用，人类甚至就无法相互了解。这是极其重要的一点，也许你们的用语“设身处地”最贴近这个意思吧。", "en": "Without any use of this fifth inner sense no man would even come close to understanding another. This is an extremely important point, and perhaps your phrase “to put yourself in someone else’s place,” most clearly approximates this sense.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第38节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "38", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "九种内在感官（下）：第六到第九", "note": "第六种是天生知识：它关系到存有对宇宙基本生命力的内在运作知识，没有它就不可能操纵生命力的材料——好比事物之间若没有先具备内在平衡感，人就不可能直立¹。要纠正一个流行说法：人类常把它跟本能混为一谈、干脆叫它本能，但它只是一种内在知识，用来操纵能量、让能量从一种形式转换成另一种形式；蜘蛛比你们更熟悉用纯净的方式来使用它²。\n\n第七种让组织囊膨胀或收缩：理论上，膨胀或收缩的允许程度并没有限制，但实际上往往是有明确限制的³。当晚课前鲁柏经验到的奇怪感觉，赛斯直接认作第七种感官的体验——只是一小部分：它代表扩大、开放或延展，是自我界限的放宽、意识理解力的扩大⁴。\n\n第八种叫解套（disentanglement）：它是最基本的内在感官之一，虽然在你们层面鲜少会完全解套，但通过训练是可能实现的——变化会发生，但通常会保留一些残留的伪装数据⁵。\n\n第九种最容易被漏：想要在你们的层面化为物质的能量人格，经由扩散（diffusion）过程——这就是第九个内在感官——先把自己扩散到很多部分里，才可能成为这个层面的一份子⁶；它的对偶紧跟着：解套的内在感官代表一个几乎和最初的扩散相反的行动，它一定要被执行，才能从你们的层面成就任何独立⁷。\n\n到后来还添了一种「直接认知」，用物质的说法可以叫遥感：你的肉体及你物质的存在，是建立在某种直接认知上，而它即推理心本身的作用的由来⁸——同一节还反过来质疑「动物透过简单的本能行为运作」那种说法：按那推理蜘蛛织网不算成就，可按同样的推理，你也得补说人在他的智力上没有功劳可言，因为人必须思考、而他不得不这样做⁸。", "src": "第 38、39、40、43、50、908 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0199", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第38节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0209", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第40节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0210", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第40节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0204", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第39节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0232", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第43节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0258", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第50节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0259", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第50节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0476", "label": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第908节"}], "groups": [{"label": "第六种 · 对基本生命力的天生知识", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0199", "zh": "第六种内在感官，关系到存有对宇宙基本生命力的内在运作知识，没有它，就不可能操纵生命力的材料。好比说，在物质宇宙里，要是你们在事物之间没有先具备内在的平衡感，就不可能直立一样。", "en": "This sixth inner sense is concerned with the entity’s innate working knowledge of the basic vitality of the universe, without which no manipulation of vitality stuff would be possible. As, for example, you could not stand up straight in your physical universe without first having among other things an innate sense of balance.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第38节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "38", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0209", "zh": "第六种内在感官是一种会利用其他可能性的基本感官之一。人类常常把它跟本能混淆在一起，也称呼它为本能。它只是一种内在知识而已，利用这种知识，可以来操纵能量，让能量从某种形式转换成另外一种形式，并让你们可以持续使用它。蜘蛛比你们更熟悉用纯净的方式来使用它。也就是说，它比人类还熟悉。", "en": "This sixth sense is one of the basic ones which makes use of the others possible. Mankind often confuses it with, and calls it, instinct. It is merely the innate knowledge which makes manipulation of energy from one form to another possible, and you use it constantly. The spider is more familiar with it in its pure form than you are. That is, than mankind is.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第40节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "40", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "第七种 · 组织囊的扩张或收缩", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0204", "zh": "因为你们今天晚上觉得不舒服，所以我晚上实际给你们的，只是我们下一节要用的大纲而已。刚刚课前鲁柏经验到的奇怪感觉，是第七种感官的体验，但只是一小部分而已。它代表扩大、开放或延展。这会从两个方向来运作。扩大或延展的目的，我下一节会讨论。它当然是一种自我的扩大或延展，以及自我界限的放宽，甚至是意识理解力的扩大、开放或延展。", "en": "What I am actually giving you this evening is an outline for our next session, since you are not up to par this evening. Now, the strange sensation experienced by Ruburt just before this session was a taste of our seventh inner sense, but only a small portion. It represents enlargement or an opening up and extension. This operates in two directions. The purpose of the enlargement or extension I will discuss at the next session. It is of course an enlargement or extension of the self, and a widening of the boundaries of the self, and therefore of even conscious comprehension.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第39节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "39", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0210", "zh": "既然我们已经简要讨论过组织囊的意义，那我将稍微再深入一点谈谈第七种内在感官。这种感官可以让组织囊膨胀或收缩。理论上，膨胀或收缩的允许程度并没有限制，但实际上往往是有明确限制的。", "en": "Now that we have briefly discussed the meaning of a tissue capsule I will go into the seventh inner sense a bit more deeply. This sense allows for an expansion or contraction of the tissue capsule. Theoretically there is no limit to the contraction or expansion allowed, but practically there are usually definite limitations.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第40节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "40", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "第八种 · 解套", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0232", "zh": "鲁柏是正确的。我们把第八种内在感官叫做解套（disentanglement）的内在感官；它是最基本的内在感官之一。虽然在你们层面鲜少会完全解套，但通过训练是可能实现的。变化会发生，但通常会保留一些残留的伪装数据。", "en": "Ruburt was right. We shall call the eighth inner sense the sense of disentanglement; and it is one of the most basic inner senses. Complete disentanglement comes rarely on your plane, although it is possible to achieve it with training. Variations occur but usually some remnant of camouflage data is retained.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "第九种 · 扩散", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0258", "zh": "想要在你们的层面化为物质的能量人格，他自己透过内在感官的运用成为这个层面的一份子。经由扩散（diffusion）过程——顺便说一下这就是我们的第九个内在感官——能量人格先把自己扩散到很多部分里。因为进入这个层面成为这个层面的一个成员，用其他方式是做不到的，所以一定要用最简单的方式，而且要建立在你们的层面上，你们的精子（sperm）当然是这方面的一个入口。", "en": "The energy personality who desires to be materialized upon your plane, himself becomes part of this plane through the use of the inner senses. Through a process of diffusion—and this incidentally is our ninth inner sense—the energy personality first diffuses himself into many parts. Since entry into this plane, as a member of this plane, cannot be made in any other manner, it must be made in the simplest terms and be built up on your plane, your sperm being of course an entry in this respect.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第50节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "50", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0259", "zh": "于是这个人格的能量必须重新组合，然后聚合，用的是我已经详细说明过的方式。解套的内在感官，以前我简略提过，代表一个几乎和最初的扩散相反的行动，它一定要被执行，才能从你们的层面成就任何独立。", "en": "The energy of the personality must then be recombined and brought together, as is done in the manner which I have specified. The inner sense of disentanglement, which I have mentioned briefly in the past, represents almost an opposing movement to the initial diffusion, and must be carried out to achieve any independence from your plane.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第50节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "50", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "后来的补充：直接认知（遥感）", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0476", "zh": "直接认知是一种内在感官，以物质的说法，你可以称之为遥感（remote sensing）。你的肉体及你物质的存在，是建立在某种直接认知上，而它即推理心本身的作用的由来。科学家喜欢说动物透过简单的本能行为运作，没有意志力：蜘蛛织网，海狸筑坝，鸟做窝，都不算是成就，因为按照这种推理，这种生物不能不这样做。蜘蛛必须织网，如果它选择不织，它就无法存活。但以那同样的推理——当然，我不附从它——你应该也补上说，人在他的智力上也没有功劳可言，因为人必须思考，而他不得不这样做。", "en": "Direct cognition is an inner sense. In physical terms you might call it remote sensing. Your physical body, and your physical existence, are based upon certain kinds of direct cognition, and it is responsible for the very functioning of the reasoning mind itself. Scientists like to say that animals operate through simple instinctive behavior, without will or volition: It is no accomplishment for a spider to make its web, a beaver its dam, a bird its nest, because according to such reasoning, such creatures cannot perform otherwise. The spider must spin his web. If he chooses not to, he will not survive. But by that same reasoning—to which, of course, I do not subscribe—you should also add that man can take no credit either for his intellect, since man must think, and cannot help doing so.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第908节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "908", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "如何主动运用", "note": "起步点指定得很明白：「要像我说过的那样，尝试使用心理时间」——在你们这个阶段，它是其他所有内在资料必经的通道¹。配套的心理前置动作是：让心智放掉钟表时间，这是你在这种情况下能够并应该允许自己的一个自由；「持续时间」则是在与心理时间的关系中、并在其架构之内被经验²。\n\n成体系的作法四段要连着读：每件东西都是暗的，静下来，尽可能生动地想象内在感官的存在，暂且假装它们与你的肉体感官相应；从你心中除去所有的思绪与忧虑，保持接纳的心情轻轻地倾听——不是听实质的声音，而是由内在感官来的声音³。影像可能会出现：接受它们像肉眼所见的东西一样确切；假装有一个内在世界，而当你学着用这些内在感官去感知它时，它会对你显现出来⁴。再假装你这一辈子对这内在世界一直是盲目的，现在才慢慢在其中看到东西——不要用你最初可能感知的不连贯的影像或最初听到的声音来判断整个的内在世界，因为你还在相当不完美地运用你的内在感官⁵。剂量是开头每天做十分钟相当够了⁶；这套书中的资料到某程度就是透过出神状态的内在感官而来，是极度有组织的内在精确性与训练的结果——而当鲁柏强烈地贯注于物质环境时，资料就不能被转译或诠释⁶。\n\n意图要先说清楚：如果你在寻求未来的信息，就应当在心里说明这一点；如果只是笼统地试着运用内在感官，那也在心里说明这一点——无论如何，鲜活程度等等通常都可以照同样的眼光来解读⁷。\n\n态度与纪律另有五条。纪律在内在感官的运用中甚至比你们认为的还重要，聚焦在内在实相有时必须暂时减少外在的聚焦，但让内在感官与外在感官同时运作是非常有可能的，只要多加练习⁸。当自我只成为一个观察者而不是控制者、且能暂时停止判断时，内在直接经验就可以获得自由⁹。更软的说法是：你们不能完全取代它，除非把自己置于危险之中——但可以学着哄骗它，偶尔不要聚焦在它上面，而让内在感官通过自我的眼睛向外看¹⁰。重心其实早就挪开了：你自己的发展和你自己吸收的速度将会是准则，你通过使用内在感官不断地移动伪装物体而不需要自己有意识的知识——「诀窍不在于学会怎么做，而在于认清发生的事」¹¹。最实用的叮嘱收尾：别没耐心，当你继续这个练习一段时间之后，你会能走得更远，而当你变得对自己内心的感受更熟悉时，就会有自己的方向感；当你向另一「台」接近时，内在的感官资料会变得越来越清楚¹²。", "src": "早期课第1册第 22、24、34、35、37、42 节；灵魂永生第 522 节；早期课第9册第 437 节；未知的实相卷二第 716 节；早期课第2册第 43 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0155", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第35节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0075", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0428", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第522节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0429", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第522节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0430", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第522节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0431", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第522节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0403", "label": "早期课第9册 · 第437节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0133", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第34节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-021-e0224", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第42节"}, {"n": 10, "id": "q-concept-021-e0177", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第37节"}, {"n": 11, "id": "q-concept-021-e0233", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第43节"}, {"n": 12, "id": "q-concept-021-e0456", "label": "未知的实相卷二 · 第716节"}], "groups": [{"label": "起步：先走心理时间", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0155", "zh": "今天晚上，我不想再探讨其他内在感官的资料了，因为现在开始说第四种内在感官为时已晚。要像我说过的那样，尝试使用心理时间。这是非常有价值的，因为在你们的这个阶段，它是其他所有内在资料必经的通道。", "en": "I do not want to go into other inner sense material this evening as it is too late to begin on the fourth inner sense. Try and use psychological time as I have told you. This is extremely valuable, for it is the channel through which all other inner data must come at your particular stage.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0075", "zh": "至于说到内在感官的通讯，我想多说一些关于“持续时间”的概念。我说过，“持续时间”可以在与心理时间的关系中，并在其架构之内被经验。这里有件重要，而且恐怕对你而言有困难的事情是，让心智放掉钟表时间。这是你在这种情况下能够并应该允许自己的一个自由。", "en": "I wanted to say a little more about duration, as far as communication from the inner senses are concerned. As I said, duration can be experienced in relation to psychological time and within its framework. The important thing here, and I’m afraid the difficult thing for you here, is the relaxation of the mind from clock time. And this is a freedom which you can and should allow yourself in such instances.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0053", "zh": "你昨日的经验，约瑟，是内在感官的练习，你应该要一而再，再而三的去尝试。", "en": "Your experience yesterday Joseph was an exercise of the inner senses, and one that you should try for again and again.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第22节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "22", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "《灵魂永生》第 522 节的练习", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0428", "zh": "每件东西都是暗的。静下来，尽可能生动地想象内在感官的存在，暂且假装它们与你的肉体感官相应。从你心中除去所有的思绪与忧虑。保持接纳的心情，轻轻地倾听，不是听实质的声音，而是由内在感官来的声音。", "en": "Everything is dark. Be quiet. Imagine as vividly as you can the existence of inner senses. For now pretend that they correspond to your physical ones. Clear from your mind all thoughts and worries. Be receptive. Very gently listen, not to physical sounds but to sounds that come through the inner senses.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第522节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "522", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0429", "zh": "影像可能会出现。接受它们像肉眼所见的东西一样的确切。假装有一个内在世界，而当你学着用这些内在感官去感知它时，它会对你显现出来。", "en": "Images may begin to appear. Accept them as sights quite as valid as those you see physically. Pretend that there is an inner world, and that it will be revealed to you as you learn to perceive it with these inner senses.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第522节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "522", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0430", "zh": "假装你这一辈子对这内在世界一直是盲目的，现在才慢慢的在其中看到东西。不要用你最初可能感知的不连贯的影像或最初听到的声音来判断整个的内在世界，因为你还在相当不完美地运用你的内在感官。", "en": "Pretend that you have been blind to this world all your life, and are now slowly gaining sight within it. Do not judge the whole inner world by the disjointed images that you may at first perceive, or by the sounds that you may at first hear, for you will still be using your inner senses quite imperfectly.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第522节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "522", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0431", "zh": "一开始每天做十分钟相当够了。现在在我写此书时，书中的资料到某程度就是透过这个在出神状态的女人的内在感官而来。这种工作是极度有组织的内在精确性与训练的结果。在鲁柏强烈地贯注于物质环境时，她不能由我这里得到资料，资料不能被转译或诠释。 因此内在感官是在各种不同的存在次元之间提供通讯的管道，然则即使如此，当资料被转译为具体形式时仍免不了有某种程度的扭曲。不然的话，它根本完全不能被感知。", "en": "Ten minutes a day to begin with is quite sufficient. Now the information in this book is being directed to some extent through the inner senses of the woman who is in trance as I write it. Such endeavor is the result of highly organized inner precision, and of training. Ruburt could not receive the information from me, it could not be translated nor interpreted while she was focused intensely in the physical environment. So the inner senses are channels that provide communication between various dimensions of existence. Yet even here the information must be distorted to some extent as it is translated into physical terms. Otherwise it would not be perceived at all.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第522节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "522", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "意图、态度、纪律与剂量", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0403", "zh": "如果你在寻求未来的信息，你就应当在心里说明这一点。这有助于把你内在的专注聚焦在想要的方向上。如果你只是在练习、笼统地试着运用内在感官，那也在心里说明这一点。无论如何，鲜活程度等等通常都可以照同样的眼光来解读。", "en": "If you are seeking future information, then you should mentally state this. It helps to focus your inner concentration along the desired lines. If you are simply exercising, trying to use the inner senses generally, then state this mentally, also. The vividness and so forth usually may be interpreted in the same light, regardless.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第437节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "437", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0456", "zh": "别没耐心。当你继续这个练习一段时间之后，你会能走得更远，而当你变得对你自己内心的感受更熟悉时，就会有自己的方向感。渐渐的，当你向另一“台”接近时，你会发现这内在的感官资料会变得越来越清楚。它会代表由一个不同的意识状态感知的实相。", "en": "Do not be impatient. As you continue with this exercise over a period of time you will be able to go further away, orienting yourself as you grow more familiar with the feeling of your mind. Gradually you will discover that this inner sense data will become clearer and clearer as you move toward another “station.” It will represent reality as perceived from a different state of consciousness.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第716节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "716", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0133", "zh": "我正要说，纪律在内在感官的运用中，甚至比你们认为的还重要。要聚焦在内在实相中，有时候必须暂时减少外在的聚焦，这时候偶尔会出现放下的样子，但内在的专注需要纪律与意图。让内在感官与外在感官同时运作是非常有可能的。只要多加练习就可以。", "en": "I was going to say that discipline is even more important in the use of the inner senses than you might think. It is true that focusing upon the inner reality at times requires a temporary lessening of outer focus, and this would sometimes give the appearance of letting go, but the inner concentration requires discipline and intent. It is quite possible to let the inner and the outer senses operate at the same time. It merely takes practice.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第34节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "34", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0224", "zh": "当自我只成为一个观察者，而不是控制者且能暂时停止判断时，内在直接经验就可以获得自由，但自我仍可以觉察到它。当自我完全或几乎完全被征服的时候，例如在睡觉时，就会有透过内在感官而来的直接经验，且意识上不会觉察到。", "en": "When the ego becomes a mere observer rather than a controller, and momentarily suspends its rigid judgments, then inner direct experience is given some freedom and yet the ego is still aware of it. When the ego is completely or nearly completely subjugated, as in sleep, then there is direct experience through the inner senses, but no conscious awareness of it.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第42节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "42", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0177", "zh": "你们不能完全取代它，除非你们把自己置于危险之中。不过你可以学着哄骗它。学会偶尔不要聚焦在它上面，而让内在感官通过自我的眼睛向外看。", "en": "You cannot displace it completely, except at your own peril. Nevertheless you can learn to trick it. You can learn to cease focusing now and then and let the inner senses look out through the ego's eyes.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0233", "zh": "我不会给你们上任何飘浮的课，不会比我在千里眼方面给鲁柏的课还多。就伪装物体穿过伪装空间来说，你自己的发展和你自己吸收的速度将会是准则。再一次，你正在和伪装打交道。你通过使用你的内在感官不断地移动伪装物体，而不需要你自己有意识的知识。诀窍不在于学会怎么做，而在于认清发生的事，经过练习这是可能的。", "en": "I am not going to give you any lessons for levitation, any more than I gave Ruburt lessons in clairvoyance. Your own development and your own rate of assimilation will be the rule, as far as the movement of camouflage objects through camouflage space is concerned. Again, you are dealing with camouflage. You move camouflage objects through the use of your inner senses constantly without your own conscious knowledge. The trick is not to learn how, but to recognize the occurrence, and with practice this is possible.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "梦与出体：内在感官的主场", "note": "这一块的判断是：不必练也已经在用的现场就是梦。说得最重的一句：你的梦世界实际上比你的醒时世界更接近实相的直接经验——在醒时世界，你内在感官的运作被屏蔽起来，以至于脱离了你自己的意识；这并不是说梦世界对你更重要，只是说它包含更多与你存在源头有关的真相¹。能量面的解释是：生命力或生命转化成物质的通道，当然是内在感官的能力；意识自我常常会阻挡很多能量，但在梦里，这种阻挡会降至最低的程度²。梦中那种经历了很多小时甚至好几天的感觉，来自在睡眠以及意识安静时运作的心理时间——这些你似乎在梦中经历的几天或几个小时，并没有被你们的身体记录下来³。\n\n投射状态是自由最大的场合：内在感官在投射状态中得以拥有最大的自由，全我获得其他情况下无法获得的经验；当这个知识变成平常醒时意识的一部分时——当你发觉你所做的事时——你就已经往前迈出巨大的一步⁴。一段很实用的归因是：在较深的梦里和相当不寻常的出体投射里，你们能够完全离开你们自己的系统，然而即使出了物质身体，你们仍会试图用那套学来的模式来转译经验，而不会切换到内在感官——这就是为什么许多这类经验，即使回想起来也显得混乱而无意义⁵。\n\n梦与出体被直接列为内在感官的使用现场，还要从现场拉回醒时：当你的眼睛睁开时，不要视为当然只有此刻可见的物体存在——向那好像没有东西的空处看看，在无声中倾听；在梦境里你用你的内在感官，而在醒时你却忽略了它们⁶。材料的来路也交代了：梦的启迪和本质被传给了那个你透过梦的形成而认识到的「自己」，你们的梦最终由这个较大的经验形成，而这经验使你涉入了一种旅程⁷。\n\n儿童也要算进来：儿童做梦时和成人一样地利用内在感官，而后透过做梦学会把这种数据转译为外在感官的精确架构——儿童的游戏永远是「在当下」，虽然其中的事件可能涉及未来或过去⁸。另有一段常被当奇谈读、其实是在讲感知框架的文字：我们没有会生长的花，但心理天性中强烈而浓缩的心灵力量会形成新的活动次元；如果在三次元中画一幅画，那画必然在一个平面上，仅只暗示了你无法插进去的那个完全三次元的经验⁹。", "src": "第 24、31、43、274、467、515、539、788、793 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0240", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第43节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0112", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第31节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0072", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0375", "label": "早期课第6册 · 第274节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0404", "label": "早期课第9册 · 第467节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0433", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第539节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0465", "label": "心灵的本质 · 第788节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0468", "label": "心灵的本质 · 第793节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-021-e0419", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第515节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0240", "zh": "在某些方面，你知道，你的梦世界，实际上比你的醒时世界，更接近实相的直接经验，在醒时世界，你内在感官的运作被屏蔽起来，以至于脱离了你自己的意识。这并不是说，在你当下的情况中，梦世界对你更重要，而只是说，它包含更多你自己的存在源头有关的真相。", "en": "In some ways you see, your dream world is actually much closer to the direct experience of reality than is your waking world, where the operation of the inner senses is shielded so from your own awareness. This is not to say that the dream world is more important to you in your present situation, merely that it contains more truth about the source of your own existence.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0112", "zh": "在最后一次的分析中提到，就意识自我而言，生命力或生命转化成为物质的通道，当然是内在感官的能力。意识自我常常会阻挡很多能量，但在梦里，这种阻挡会降至最低的程度。", "en": "In the last analysis the channel for vitality or for vitality’s transformation into physical matter is of course the inner senses’ ability, and there is a counteraction here as far as the conscious ego is concerned. The conscious ego often blocks much energy. In dreams the blocking is minimized.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第31节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "31", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0072", "zh": "任何来自内在感官的这种通讯，都会存在你们的心理时间。我也说过这个心理时间，在睡眠以及意识安静时运作。现在，在梦中以及在梦的架构中，你有一种经历了很多小时、甚至好几天的感觉。这些你似乎在梦中经历的几天或几个小时，并没有被你们的身体所记录下来，并且是在你们物理时间的伪装之外。如果在一个梦里，比如说，你在这个梦架构内经历了两天的时间，你在身体上并没有变老两天。", "en": "Any such communications coming through the inner senses will exist in your psychological time. I have said also that this psychological time operates during sleep and during quiet times of consciousness. Now in dreams and in the dream framework you have the feeling of experiencing many hours, or even days. These days or hours that you seem to experience in dreams are not recorded by the physical body, and are outside of your physical time camouflage. If in a dream for example you experience within the framework two days, physically you do not age for these two days.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0375", "zh": "投射涉及全我的面向还有很多，是人格在许多重要方面正进步中的一个标记。内在感官在投射状态中得以拥有最大的自由，而且全我获得其他情况下无法获得的经验。当这个知识变成平常醒时意识的一部分时，也就是说，当你发觉你所做的事时，你就已经往前迈出巨大的一步。", "en": "Projections involve many more aspects of the whole self, and are a mark that the personality is progressing in important ways. The inner senses are allowed their greatest freedom in projection states, and the whole self retains experience that it would not otherwise. When this knowledge becomes part of the usual waking consciousness, that is when you realize what you have done, then you have taken a gigantic step forward.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第274节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "274", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0404", "zh": "在较深的梦里和相当不寻常的出体投射里，你们能够——而且确实——完全离开你们自己的系统。然而即使出了物质身体，你们仍会试图用那套学来的模式来转译经验，而不会切换到内在感官。这就是为什么许多这类经验，即使回想起来，也显得混乱而无意义。", "en": "In deeper dreams and fairly unusual projections, you can and do leave your own system entirely. Even though you are out of your physical body however, you will attempt to translate experience with its learned patterns rather than switching into the inner senses. This is why many such experiences, even if recalled, seem chaotic and without meaning.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第467节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "467", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0433", "zh": "当你的眼睛睁开时，不要视为当然只有此刻可见的物体存在。向那好像没有东西的空处看看，在无声中倾听。在无物的空间里每一寸都有分子的结构，但你却叫自己看不见它们。还有其他的声音，但你已制约了你的耳朵让它们听不见那些声音。在梦境里你用你的内在感官，而在醒时你却忽略了它们。", "en": "When your eyes are open, do not take it for granted that only the immediately perceivable objects exist. Look where space seems empty, and listen in the middle of silence. There are molecular structures in every inch of empty space, but you have taught yourself not to perceive them. There are other voices, but you have conditioned your ears not to hear them. You use your inner senses when you are in the dream state, and ignore them when you are waking.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第539节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "539", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0465", "zh": "这只不过是一个比喻，因为你经常沉湎于那另一个实相里：但它的启迪和本质，被传给了你「自己」，这个自己是你透过梦的形成而认识到的，而以你们的话说，「做梦要花时间」。你们的梦最终由这个较大的经验形成，而这经验使你涉入了一种旅程。用另一种比喻，那就像是你愉快地把日常生活的正常行头留在后面，而驾着你自己较大的心灵，驶入更广大的经验之海。 你离开了事件的实质本质，而进入那些事件在其中形成的区域。以最难描写的方式，你利用远较广范围的内在感官（inner sense），而以一种更直接的方式接触宇宙。", "en": "This is simply an analogy because you are steeped in that other reality constantly; but its illuminations and nature are transmitted to the self that you know through the formation of dreams, and in your terms, “it takes time to dream.” This larger experience, from which your dreams are finally formed, involves you in a kind of journey. Period. Using another analogy, it is as if you joyfully leave the normal paraphernalia of usual life behind, and ride aboard your own greater psyche into vaster seas of experience.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第788节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "788", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0468", "zh": "当儿童做梦时，他们如成人一样地利用内在感官，而后透过做梦，他们学会把这种数据转译为外在感官的精确架构。儿童的游戏永远是「在当下」——游戏是立即被体验的，虽然其中的事件可能涉及未来或过去。「从前有个时候」这句子是极具感召性的，即使对成人也是，因为儿童以一种成人已遗忘的方式与时间游戏。如果你要感觉你心灵的动作，也许最简单的是想象一个情况，或在过去或在未来，因为这自动地以一种新的方式移动你精神性的感官知觉（sense perception）。", "en": "When children dream, they utilize these inner senses as adults do, and then through dreaming they learn to translate such material into the precise framework of the exterior senses. Children’s games are always “in the present” — that is, they are immediately experienced, though the play events may involve the future or the past. The phrase “once upon a time” is strongly evocative and moving, even to adults, because children play with time in a way that adults have forgotten. If you want to sense the motion of your psyche, it is perhaps easiest to imagine a situation either in the past or the future, for this automatically moves your mental sense-perceptions in a new way.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第793节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "793", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0419", "zh": "我们赋予我们环境中的元素更大的创造力，那是难以解释的。举例来说，我们没有会生长的花，但我们心理天性中强烈而浓缩的心灵力量会形成新的活动次元。如果你在三次元的存在中画一副画，那么这画必然是在个平面上，仅只暗示了你无法插进去的那个完全三次元的经验。然而，在我们的环境，我们能够创造我们所想要的任何次元的效果。这些能力并非我们所独有，而也是你们的遗产。在这本书里，你以后会看到，在你其他的意识状态中，而非正式的、清醒的状态中，你比你以为的要更常常在练习运用你自己的内在感官及多次元的能力。", "en": "We endow the elements of our environment with an even greater creativity that is difficult to explain. We do not have flowers that grow, for example. But the intensity, the condensed psychic strength of our psychological natures forms new dimensions of activity. If you paint a picture within three-dimensional existence, then the painting must be on a flat surface, merely hinting at the complete three-dimensional experience that you cannot insert into it. In our environment, however, we could actually create whatever dimensional effects we desired. All of these abilities are not ours alone. They are your heritage. As you will see later in this book, you exercise your own inner senses, and multidimensional abilities, more frequently than it might seem, in other states of consciousness than the normal, waking one.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "515", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "直觉、灵感与创造", "note": "顺序在这里是定死的，这是本块的骨架：意念源自潜意识是事实，但在这之前，「意念特质」会被内在感官接收到——有时候，它以直觉的方式被接收到，灵光乍现于意识心¹。更急一点的说法：内在感官试图拼命地向个体解释它们的知识，它会透过你们叫作预感或直觉的东西来传达——那代表一种确切而抹不掉的、实相的实际知识²。推到宗教经验那一侧：「一切万有」的本质只能透过内在感官来直接感觉，或在一个较弱的沟通里，透过灵感或直觉来感受它³。\n\n爱因斯坦是现成的例子：他在他自己的直觉之内旅行，并且信任它们，他也运用他的内在感官——如果当初他能够更加信任自己的直觉、把证明理论的更多所谓科学证据给更少的人、让自己得到更多内在的自由，那他的发现会更多⁴。\n\n创造这一侧同样落在使用现场：当你画一幅画时，你在处理能量的转换与伪装模式的转换——在这样一种创造行动中，有一刻，短暂但重要的一刻，你在处理底下的生命力⁵；那棵消失的树并没有真正消失：为了已经开始动手的画作，用你的内在感官在心中创建那棵树，在画作中它就会成为一棵更好的树，因为你有能力创造树的本质⁶。\n\n范围还要放大：约瑟透过内在视象接收到许多资讯，过去他或多或少自动把这个资讯转译成新的伪装模式——转换成绘画——但他并没有认识到他接收到任何视象⁷；诗一直都是使用内在感官能力的结果，而《物质世界即意念建构》那首诗代表着珍那边的一个突破⁸。判断收束：直觉、灵感、预感与创作冲动不是另外几件事，而是同一套感官在意识边缘的几种显形。", "src": "第 19、22、23、31、35、37、45、565 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0111", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第31节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0179", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第37节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0437", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第565节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0246", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第45节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0022", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第19节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0137", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第35节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0049", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第22节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0057", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第23节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0111", "zh": "这些模式按照一定的法则而演化。它们只是反映其背后的意念而已，而你必须认识到，这些意念源自不同的源头。它们起源于潜意识，这是事实，但是在这之前，意念特质（idea quality）会被内在感官接收到。有时候，意念特质会以直觉的方式被接收到，灵光乍现于意识心。意识自我（conscious ego）是伪装模式的主要操纵者，也是明显的执行者。生命力是形成伪装模式的实际材料，它存在着，而且被你们的人格无意识地运用。", "en": "The patterns evolve according to certain laws. They merely reflect the ideas behind them, and these ideas you must realize originate from different sources. They originate in the subconscious, it is true, but before this an idea quality is received by the inner senses. Sometimes this idea quality is received as intuition, where it sparks into the conscious mind. But the conscious ego is the primary manipulator of camouflage patterns and the obvious mover. The actual material from which camouflage patterns are formed is the vitality which exists and which is unconsciously used by your personalities.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第31节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "31", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0179", "zh": "内在感官试图拼命地向个体解释它们的知识。它会透过你们叫作预感或直觉的东西来传达。它代表一种确切并抹不掉的、实相的实际知识。", "en": "The inner senses try desperately to make their knowledge plain to the individual. It is communicated through what you call hunch or intuition. It represents actual knowledge of a definite and inerasable reality.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0437", "zh": "“一切万有”的本质只能透过“内在感官”来直接感觉，或在一个较弱的沟通里，则可以透过灵感或直觉来感受它。这种实相之不可思议的复杂性无法以语言来诠释。", "en": "The nature of All That Is can only be sensed directly through the inner senses, or, in a weaker communication, through inspiration or intuition. The miraculous complexity of such reality cannot be translated verbally.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第565节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "565", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0246", "zh": "爱因斯坦在他自己的直觉之内旅行，并且信任它们，他也运用他的内在感官。如果当初他能够更加信任自己的直觉，把证明他理论的更多所谓的科学证据给更少的人，让他自己得到更多内在的自由，那他的发现会更多。", "en": "Einstein traveled within, and trusted, his own intuitions, and used his inner senses. He would have discovered much more had he been able to trust his intuitions even more, and able to leave more of the so-called scientific proof of his theories to lesser men, to give himself more inner freedom.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第45节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "45", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0049", "zh": "的确，约瑟透过内在视象接收到许多资讯。过去，他或多或少地自动把这个资讯转译成新的伪装模式，换句话说，就是转换成绘画，但是他并没有认识到他接收到任何视象。约瑟，随着我告诉你更多的内在感官的事，你可以学着运用你其他的内在感官。", "en": "It is true that Joseph receives much data through inner visions. In the past he has more or less translated this data automatically into a new camouflage pattern, in other words into a painting, without realizing that he had received any vision at all. You can learn, Joseph, to use your other inner senses as I tell you more about them.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第22节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "22", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0137", "zh": "你们的树消失了，我很遗憾，然而我们都知道，这棵树并没有真正消失。我希望你会为了你已经开始动手的画作，使用你的内在感官，在心中创建那棵树。然后，在画作中，它就会成为一棵更好的树，因为你有能力创造树的本质。", "en": "I am sorry that your tree has vanished, yet we all know that the tree has not really vanished. And I hope that you will use your inner senses to create the tree in your mind for the painting that you have begun. Now it will be a better tree in the painting, for you will be able to create the essence of the tree.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0022", "zh": "就这个讨论来说，你自己的创作经验应该对你很有用。我亲爱的自负的约瑟，当你画一幅画时，你在处理能量的转换与伪装模式的转换。在这样一种创造行动中，有一刻，短暂但重要的一刻，你在处理我说过的底下的生命力。由于你们地球的物质情境，你被迫将这创造能量转变成另一种伪装模式。你没有别的办法，但是在这一刻，你从内在感官摘取这个生命力，用双手抓住这个燃料。你拥有它。你把它转变成稍微不同、更有启发作用的一个新伪装模式，但是比平常的模式更流畅、更不固定，因而赋予基本燃料或生命力本身更大的自由和机动性。你接近一种跨层移民（transmigration of planes.）", "en": "Your own experience with creativity should serve you well as far as this discussion goes. When you paint a picture, my dear egotistical Joseph, you are dealing with a transformation of energy and a transformation of camouflage pattern. There is a moment, a brief but vital moment in such an act of creation, when you are dealing with the underlying vitality of which I have spoken. You are forced because of your earthly physical situation to transform this creative energy into another camouflage pattern. There is nothing else you can do. But for this moment you pluck this vitality from the inner senses, you grab ahold of this fuel with both hands. You have it. You transform it into a somewhat different more evocative new camouflage pattern that is nevertheless more fluent, more fluid, than the usual pattern, and which gives greater freedom and mobility to the basic fuel or vitality itself. You approach a transmigration of planes.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第19节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "19", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0057", "zh": "诗一直都是使用内在感官能力的结果，但直到最近，他都还不能给出这种单一形式的充分模式。他在《物质世界即意念建构》（The Physical World as Idea Construction）一书中的努力，代表着他这边的一个突破。我相信，从一开始他就认识到，有意识的批判性思维和最初的概念没有任何关系。", "en": "The poetry has always been the result of facility in use of the inner senses, but until lately he was unable to give this sufficient pattern in terms of unitary form. His efforts in the book The Physical World as Idea Construction represented a breakthrough on his part. He realized, I believe, from the beginning that the conscious critical mind had little to do with the initial conception.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "常见误解与警示", "note": "第一类是把它神秘化。指导灵、灵媒等诸如此类的，从一开始就是荒谬可笑的——你只是在使用内在感官而已；这些感官并不神奇，不管怎样定义宗教，它们当然也没有宗教的意味，赛斯也不是鲁柏某个退化的次人格¹。同思路再补一刀：这次会面以及你们和马克做的实验都不是降神会——所谓的降神会，要是确有其事，都只是使用内在感官的练习而已²。术语也更正过：超感官知觉充其量只是一个蹩脚的词，「内在感官知觉」会是一个精准得多的描述³。\n\n第二类是把五官当验收标准，这是出现频率最高的障碍。机制在这里：当你坚持要透过外在的、公认的感官接受证据时，你几乎就自动地关闭了内在感官装置——这样的习惯性反应在很大程度上是人自己设定的，并不是一个自然的习惯反应；一旦你迈开这自发性的第一步，你就真的会收到证据⁴。整体来说，你们在智识上还不了解内在感官，而你们否认的那一部分自己非常了解它——于是你在一个奇怪的位置上，试图用伪装的工具解剖内在世界⁵。这从一开始就涉及一个几乎不可能完成的任务：来自内在感官的资料生动而逼真、可靠，是你们在坚持把这个资料转译成物质词语才会有困难——你不会因为你不能用双手捧着一个心理经验，就说它不存在⁶。失败的典型样子是：实际的通讯并不是用语言或图像来呈现，意识心很少体验到单纯状态的内在感官资料；你们有的是匆匆忙忙转换频道、一种企图用外在感官接收这种资料的举动——这种举动很不恰当，通常还会招来一点灾难⁷。\n\n第三类是情绪与外力。总纲是：就来自内在感官的资讯而言，有意识的恐惧通常是主要障碍——了解这些感官属于你、而且是相当自然的，就会帮助你避免意识原本无可避免的自动关闭⁸。一段第一手记录在案：一次几乎失控的经验把人吓到自动把自己断开，但整个事件是有益的，因为它给了对纯粹内在感官资讯的第一手经验；要是再出现这样的事情，就试着放松，资讯自己就会慢下来⁹。外力的警告更硬：即使不加以限制地充分运用外在感官，也能引导你们进入内在实相，但通常只有强大而有纪律的自己、一个结构完整的本体才能以这种方式感知，然而只是偶一为之——在你们这个种族现在的发展阶段，内在感官和外在感官的全面运作令人盲目¹⁰。\n\n第四类解释「为什么我们不太会用」：个人随着成长逐渐信赖外在感官到一个很大的程度，并逐渐丧失对内在感官的依赖——而那些内在感官是他们更熟悉的、在婴幼儿及孩童时期主要利用的感官；仍有一些人坚持继续这古老而基本的依赖，这些个人体现的就是一个开放的系统¹¹。", "src": "第 20、24、25、26、29、54、78、254 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0035", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第20节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0036", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第20节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0265", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第54节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0085", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第25节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0088", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第25节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0100", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第26节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0108", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第29节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0080", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 9, "id": "q-concept-021-e0079", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第24节"}, {"n": 10, "id": "q-concept-021-e0360", "label": "早期课第6册 · 第254节"}, {"n": 11, "id": "q-concept-021-e0291", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第78节"}], "groups": [{"label": "不是鬼神，也不是 ESP", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0035", "zh": "指导灵、灵媒等诸如此类的，从一开始就是荒谬可笑的。你只是在使用内在感官而已。这些感官并不神奇，不管怎样定义宗教，它们当然也没有宗教的意味，我也不是鲁柏某个退化的次人格。我也不会被拿来跟某个长着长胡子、目光锐利、坐在九霄云外的灵相比。", "en": "The designations spirit, and medium and so forth, are ridiculous to begin with. You are simply using inner senses. These senses are not magical, they certainly are not religious in any sense of the word, and I am not some degenerating secondary personality of Ruburt's. Nor will I be compared with some long- bearded, beady-eyed spirit sitting on cloud nine.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0036", "zh": "我的确以人类的形式活过，但那也只是个事实。依据一般赋予的含意，这次会面以及我们其他的会面都不是降神会，你们和你们的朋友马克做的实验也不是降神会。所谓的降神会，要是确有其事，都只是使用内在感官的练习而已。", "en": "It is true that I have lived as a human being, but this is simply a fact. This meeting and our other meetings are not seances, and your experiments with your friend Mark are not seances, according to the implications usually given. So-called seances, when they are legitimate, are simply exercises in the use of the inner senses.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0265", "zh": "给鲁柏一个小注，关于他超感知觉的书。我希望他现在了解超感官知觉充其量只是一个蹩脚的词。内在感官知觉（Inner sense perception）会是一个精准得多的描述。虽然如此，自从他丢弃其他研究者的资料不用，转而仰赖他自己的资料，他就已经遥遥领先了。", "en": "A small note to Ruburt concerning his ESP book. I hope by now he realizes that extrasensory perception is a poor term at best. Inner sense perception would be a much more accurate description. Nevertheless, he is far ahead since he dispensed with material from other researchers, and relied upon his own.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "误区：拿五官当证据", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0085", "zh": "事实是，当你坚持要透过外在的、公认的感官接受证据时，你几乎就自动地关闭了内在感官装置。这是没有必要的。这样的习惯性反应在很大程度上是人自己设定的。这不是一个自然的习惯反应。你必须接受内在资料的千真万确，但你不会这样做。一旦你迈开这自发性的第一步，你就真的会收到、甚至是你的意识心也不得不接受的证据。但是，你必须先有这样的意愿踏出第一步。", "en": "The fact is that when you insist upon evidence through the outside, regularly accepted senses, that you almost automatically turn off the inner sense apparatus. This is not necessary. Man to a large degree has set up this habit reaction. It is not a natural habit reaction. You must take the inner data at its face value, and this is what you will not do. Once you take this first step of spontaneity, you will actually receive evidence that even your conscious mind will be forced to accept. But the first step of such willingness must be made.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第25节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "25", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0088", "zh": "确实，整体来说，你们在智识上还不了解内在感官。你们否认的那一部分自己非常了解内在感官。但在这个游戏阶段，这对你没有好处，所以你在一个奇怪的位置上，再一次试图用伪装的工具解剖内在世界。", "en": "It is true that as a whole you do not as yet understand the inner senses intellectually. The part of yourself which you deny understands the inner senses well. But this does you no good at this stage of the game and so you are in the peculiar position, once more, of trying to dissect the inner world with camouflage tools.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第25节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "25", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0100", "zh": "这从一开始就涉及一个几乎不可能完成的任务。来自内在感官的资料生动而逼真，是可靠的，并让有意识的个体留下印象。是你们在坚持把这个资料转译成物质词语，才会有困难。你并不是坚持要看、要感觉或触摸一个心理经验，但你不会说因为你不能用双手捧着它，所以心理经验就不存在。", "en": "This involves, to begin with, an almost impossible task. Data from the inner senses is vivid, it is reliable, it makes an impression upon the conscious individual. It is your insistence upon translating this material into physical terms that causes your difficulty. You do not insist upon seeing, feeling or touching a psychological experience, and yet you do not say that a psychological experience does not exist because you cannot hold it in both hands.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第26节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "26", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0108", "zh": "实际的通讯并不是用语言或图像来呈现。意识心很少体验到单纯状态的内在感官资料。你们有的是，匆匆忙忙转换频道，一种企图用外在感官接收这种资料的举动，这种举动很不恰当，通常还会招来一点灾难。", "en": "The actual communication is not in words or pictures. Material from the inner senses is very seldom experienced by the conscious mind in its pure condition. What you get is a hasty twisting of channel, a rather inept and usually somewhat disastrous attempt to pick up this material with the outer senses.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第29节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "29", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "恐惧与屏蔽", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0080", "zh": "因为你们俩都挺累的，所以我将结束这节课。还有一点我想说，首先，是这样的：就来自内在感官的资讯而言，有意识的恐惧通常是主要障碍。因此，了解这些感官属于你，而且是相当自然的，就会帮助你避免意识原本无可避免地自动关闭这种资讯。", "en": "Since you both are tiring I will end this session. The one point I would like to make, first, is this: Conscious fear is usually the main hindrance as far as data from the inner senses is concerned. Therefore, a realization that these senses belong to you and are quite natural will help you avoid the otherwise unavoidable, almost automatic closing off of such data by the consciousness.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0079", "zh": "你自动地把自己断开，因为这个经历吓坏了你，但是整个事件是有益的，因为它给了你某种对于纯粹内在感官资讯的第一手经验。遗憾的是它是如此的失控，但这恐怕在一开始都是这样的。如果可能，要是再出现这样的事情，就试着放松，资讯自己就会慢下来。", "en": "You switched yourself off automatically because the experience frightened you, but the whole affair was beneficial because it gave you some first-hand experience of pure inner sensory data. It was unfortunate that it was so uncontrolled, but I’m afraid this is to be expected in the beginning. If possible try to relax if this occurs again, and the data will slow itself up.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0360", "zh": "即使不加以限制地充分运用外在感官，也能引导你们进入内在实相。通常只有强大而有纪律的自己，一个结构完整的本体，才能以这种方式感知，然而只是偶一为之。你看，在你们这个种族现在的发展阶段，内在感官和外在感官的全面运作令人盲目，就像你阅读吸毒经验看到的那样。", "en": "Full and uninhibited use of even the outer senses would lead you to inner reality. Usually only a strong and disciplined self, a well-structured identity, can perceive in this manner, and then only occasionally. Full operation of inner and outer senses, you see, in your present stage of development as a race, would be blinding, as you can see in your reading of drug experiences.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第254节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "254", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "成长中怎么弄丢的", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0291", "zh": "一个个人随着成长逐渐信赖外在感官到一个很大的程度，并逐渐丧失对内在感官的依赖，而那些内在感官是他们更熟悉的、在他们婴幼儿及孩童时期主要利用的感官。这通常是很实际的事；但还是有一些人坚持继续这古老而基本的、对内在感官的依赖，这些个人体现的就是一个开放的系统。", "en": "As individual reliance upon the outer senses develops, the personality to a large degree relies upon them, and gradually loses the habit of relying upon the more familiar inner senses utilized mainly in infancy and childhood. This is usually a matter of practicality; yet there are those who continue stubbornly this older and basic reliance upon the inner senses, and these individuals utilize the realization of an open system.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第78节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "78", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B10", "title": "内外并用的平衡与回报", "note": "本块的判断是：发展内在感官不是出世间的事，赛斯把回报定义在两边都用得上。理想型先给出：一种善于充分运用内在和外在感官两者的意识¹。写成要求是：在伪装实相之中，外在感官要喜悦又有效地被彻底利用，应该到一个比平常大很多的程度，于是意识心得以在经验中利用它自己、进而认识它自己²；紧接着，内在感官因此也应该像外在感官一样被充分利用——在两个实相之内的经验，让内我或全我更加充分认识它自己的潜力以及它本身的个性³。\n\n最直接的定心丸：这段关系应该会让你更有能力与外在世界打交道，永远不会建议你们尝试逃避它；发展内在感官不会抹杀外在世界，它会让你们更清楚地看到外在世界是什么，因此更有能力操控伪装模式⁴。情绪也安抚到位：你们应该有很多平静的课、充满成就感——而且别忘了，训练内在感官不会对你们造成任何伤害，真正让努力大打折扣的是恐惧⁵；实际处方也包括继续出去走走、邀请朋友来家里——把重心放回物质生活⁵。\n\n身份层面的回报：运用内在感官，我们就变成有意识的创造者，或共同创造者——但不管你知道与否，你本来就是个无意识的共同创造者⁶。说得含蓄的一句是：肉身自己无法感知另外维度的实际存在，但透过内在感官，某种开悟可以被企及；也是透过内在感官，内我借由认识它自己的自由，可以得到一种信任和持续的感觉⁷。\n\n安全判断收尾：只要追随目前的方向，是不会有危险的，一旦你变了，那就会非常危险⁸；谈到实用性，如果你好好发挥并使用你的内在感官，甚至会发现，在与你们珍爱的伪装模式打交道时，它也是最有帮助的⁸。", "src": "第 18、28、37、107、130、515 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0010", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第18节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0323", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第130节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0324", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第130节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0104", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第28节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0106", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第28节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0417", "label": "灵魂永生 · 第515节"}, {"n": 7, "id": "q-concept-021-e0313", "label": "早期课第3册 · 第107节"}, {"n": 8, "id": "q-concept-021-e0180", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第37节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0010", "zh": "某些像许多植物生命和植物性生命的片段体，有大量使用特定内在感官的情形。你们的岩石，约瑟，我会称作为“植物性的”（vegetative）。岩石根本不是没有生命。其他种类的生命，包括你们自己，都依赖你们已经知道的外在感官。理想的当然是，一种善于充分运用内在和外在感官两者的一种意识。", "en": "In some fragments such as much plant life and vegetative life there is strong use of certain inner senses. Your rocks, Joseph, I will call vegetative. Rocks are far from lifeless. Other types of life, including your own, rely on the recognized outer senses. The ideal of course is a consciousness that is adept at using both the inner and outer senses fully.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第18节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "18", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0323", "zh": "这涉及到在它们的伪装实相之中的外在感官，以及在你经历某种程度存在的那个伪装场域之内喜悦又有效的行为与操纵，有效又彻底的利用。当你在它之内运作时，你真的应该尽可能在很多方面彻底体验它，应该是到一个比平常大很多的程度，于是意识心得以在经验中利用它自己，进而认识它自己。然后再转换到内在感官的运用。所以这个大反差让全我焕然一新。（停顿）", "en": "This involves efficient, complete use of the outer senses in their perception of camouflage reality, and of joyful, effective behavior and manipulation within that field of camouflage in which you spend a certain level of your existence. When you operate within it you should indeed experience it completely, in as many phases as possible, and be it to a much greater degree than is usually achieved, the conscious mind using itself then in experience, and thus knowing itself. And then the switch to use of the inner senses. The great contrast then refreshes the whole self. （Pause.）", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第130节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "130", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0324", "zh": "内在感官因此也应该像外在感官一样被充分利用。在两个实相之内的经验让内我或全我更加充分认识它自己的潜力以及它本身的个性。", "en": "The inner senses therefore should also be used as fully as the outer senses. Experience within both realities lets the inner or whole self know more fully its own potentialities and its own selfness.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第130节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "130", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0104", "zh": "我们的关系应该会让你俩更有能力与外在世界打交道。我永远不会建议你们尝试逃避它。发展你们的内在感官不会抹杀外在世界。它会让你们能够更清楚地看到外在世界是什么，因此，你们将更有能力操控伪装模式。", "en": "Our relationship should enable you both to deal more adequately with the outside world. I will never suggest that you try to escape it. Your development of the inner senses will not blot out the outer world. It will enable you to see it more clearly for what it is, and therefore you will be able to manipulate camouflage patterns more adequately.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第28节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "28", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0106", "zh": "你们应该有很多平静的课，充满成就感。我希望我们能够回到平稳的状态。而且别忘了，训练内在感官不会对你们造成任何伤害。恐惧会让你们这些努力大打折扣。我也建议你们持续练习在星期六晚上出去走走，虽然鲁柏不是个热情的女主人，但我建议你们邀请朋友来家里。约瑟你也要去散步，或至少更常外出。", "en": "You should have many quiet sessions filled with accomplishment. I hope we have things on an even keel again. And remember, no harm can come to either of you through training your inner senses. Fear can hold you back greatly in these efforts. I would also suggest continuing your practice of getting out of the house on Saturday evenings, and though Ruburt is not a passionate hostess I would suggest that you have friends in. And also that you, Joseph, take walks or at least get out more often.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第28节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "28", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0417", "zh": "运用内在感官，我们就变成有意识的创造者，或共同创造者。但不管你知道与否，你是个无意识的共同创造者。如果我们的环境对你似乎是没有结构的，那是因为你不明白秩序的真实本质，它与永久的形式完全无干，只是由你的着眼点看来是如此而已。", "en": "Using the inner senses, we become conscious creators, cocreators. But you are unconscious cocreators whether you know it or not. If our environment seems unstructured to you, it is only because you do not understand the true nature of order, which has nothing to do with permanent form, but only appears to have form from your perspective.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "515", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0313", "zh": "至于肉身自己无法感知两个维度的实际存在，透过内在感官，某种开悟可以被企及；而且也是透过内在感官，内我借由认识它自己的自由，可以得到一种信任和持续的感觉。", "en": "Through the inner senses, therefore, some enlightenment can be received as to both the actual existence of dimensions that the physical self cannot perceive; and also through the inner senses, a sense of confidence and continuity can be achieved through the inner self’s knowledge of its freedom.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第107节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "107", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0180", "zh": "你只要追随目前的方向，是不会有危险的，一旦你变了，那就会非常危险。你将发现这些还不是很确定的预言到时候就会成真。你知道自由意志永远都在运作，这早已是一个定论。我在我的道路上也很实际。谈到实用性，如果你好好发挥并使用你的内在感官，甚至会发现，在与你们珍爱的伪装模式打交道时，它也是最有帮助的。", "en": "You are in no danger however as long as you pursue your present course, but you are in peril as soon as you change it. You will find that these loose predictions will come to pass. You understand that free will always operates, this being a foregone conclusion. I also am practical in my way. And speaking of practicality, you would find it most beneficial even in dealing with your precious camouflage patterns if you would develop the use of your inner senses.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B11", "title": "不只人类有：从细胞到万物", "note": "把内在感官读成「人类的超能力」会漏掉它的定位。就运动而言，树往上和往下移动——说它无法移动自己蛮不公平的，因为它移动到一个惊人的程度，根和枝朝着四面八方移动；植物一生的内在感官都是对准频道、警醒的，这些片段体拥有的意识相当高，人居然这么轻视它们¹。再细一层：你们的树透过它的内在感官存活，体验着很多的感受，也对很多你们未觉察的刺激起反应——地球细微的震动、甚至小蚂蚁在它树干低处周边的动作，树的意识都有认知也有体验；像看不见的湿度、放射线以及地球所有的电值，都被树感知为相当真实的东西，也被认知到它们与树本身是分离的²。\n\n蜘蛛也被算进来：结网的蜘蛛是在使用它的第六种内在感官，因为这些内在感官也是其他生物的潜在特性，并不只是限于人类³。同一张网再推一步：你们的动物借助内在感官拥有更紧密的联结——蜘蛛网在时间和空间中都存在，就像所有的物质建构一样，而你们的宇宙之所以不是像蜘蛛网那样存在，正因为它不受空间和时间的限制⁴。总纲一句话把范围与关系都定了：肉体感官是内在感官的延伸，内在感官是每个具体物种的一部分，不论其程度为何；内在感官提供给所有物种一个内在的沟通方法——那么，细胞拥有内在感官⁵。\n\n最后一段要小心读：你们感知树木、山、人们、海洋，但你从未见过一个人与一颗树合而为一——这将被视为一个幻觉的形象；你们的视觉数据是被学得并被诠释的，因此它们显得好像是那些数据唯一可能的结果，而内在视像能令你惶惑，是因为你在心智中很清楚地看见那些照着学来的取法就不该看见的东西⁶。这一句是描述性的，不宜当作「万物一体」的证明段来用；它与「别拿五官当证据」恰好是同一件事的两面。", "src": "第 18、40、49、777、886 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": "q-concept-021-e0009", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第18节"}, {"n": 2, "id": "q-concept-021-e0011", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第18节"}, {"n": 3, "id": "q-concept-021-e0206", "label": "早期课第1册 · 第40节"}, {"n": 4, "id": "q-concept-021-e0256", "label": "早期课第2册 · 第49节"}, {"n": 5, "id": "q-concept-021-e0471", "label": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第886节"}, {"n": 6, "id": "q-concept-021-e0463", "label": "心灵的本质 · 第777节"}], "groups": [{"label": "动物、植物与细胞", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0009", "zh": "就运动而言，树往上和往下移动。说它无法移动自己蛮不公平的，因为它移动到一个惊人的程度，根和枝朝着四面八方移动。植物一生的内在感官都是对准频道、警醒的，而且非常重要。这些片段体拥有的意识相当高，人居然这么轻视它们。", "en": "And as far as motion is concerned, the tree moves upward and downward. It is quite unfair to say that it cannot transport itself since it does so to an amazing degree, the roots and limbs moving in all directions. The inner senses of all plant life are well attuned, alert and very important. All these fragments have consciousness to a rather high degree, considering that man holds them in such ill repute.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第18节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "18", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0011", "zh": "你们的树透过它的内在感官存活，体验着很多的感受，也对很多你们未觉察的刺激起反应。地球细微的震动，甚至小蚂蚁在它树杆低处周边的动作，树的意识都有认知也有体验。像这些看不见的湿度、放射线以及地球所有的电值，都被你们的树感知为相当真实的东西，也被认知到它们与树本身是分离的。", "en": "Your tree lives through its inner senses, experiencing many sensations and reacting to many stimuli of which you are unaware. Minute earth tremors, even the motion of small ants about its lower trunk, are recognized and experienced by tree consciousness. Such invisibilities as humidity, radioactivity and all electrical earthly values, are felt as quite real things by your tree and recognized as being separate from the tree itself.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第18节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "18", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0206", "zh": "我提过，第六种内在感官，除了是内我的一种特性外，也包含某些可以连结到你们所谓本能的东西。可以想像一下结网的蜘蛛。蜘蛛网是一种确实存在你们层面的伪装模式。这种状况下，你们那单纯的蜘蛛是在使用它的第六种内在感官，因为这些内在感官也是其他生物的潜在特性，并不只是限于人类才有。", "en": "As I mentioned, the sixth inner sense involves something that can be likened to what you call the instincts, except that it is a property of the inner self. Consider a spider spinning a web. The web is a camouflage pattern that definitely exists on your plane. Here your simple spider is using his sixth sense, for these senses are the latent property of other living things, and not restricted to mankind.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第40节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "40", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0256", "zh": "你们的动物借助内在感官拥有更紧密的联结。还记得我们的蜘蛛和蜘蛛网的比喻吧。蜘蛛网在时间和空间中都存在，就像所有的物质建构一样。这就是为什么我说你们的宇宙不是像蜘蛛网那样存在，只因为它不受空间和时间的限制。再说一次，就价值完成而言，就你们的外在感官无法理解的方式来说，宇宙一直在扩展。", "en": "Your animals possess a closer bond by means of the inner senses. Remember our analogy of the spider and its web. The web exists both in time and space, as all physical constructions do. That is why I have said that your universe does not exist in the same fashion as the web, simply because it is not bound by space or time. The universe expands, again, in terms of value fulfillment, and in ways which your outer senses cannot comprehend.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第49节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "49", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-021-e0471", "zh": "肉体感官是内在感官（inner senses）的延伸，内在感官是每个具体物种的一部分，不论其程度为何。内在感官提供给所有物种一个内在的沟通方法。那么，细胞拥有内在感官。", "en": "The physical senses are the extensions of inner senses 3 that are, in one way or another, a part of each physical species regardless of its degree. The inner senses provide all species with an inner method of communication. The c-e-l-l-s (spelled out), then, possess inner senses.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第886节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "886", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "一处要小心的读法：内在视像与被诠释的视觉数据", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-021-e0463", "zh": "不论你们的语言为何，你们感知树木、山、人们、海洋。举例来说，你从未见过一个人与一颗树合而为一。这将被视为一个幻觉的形象。你们的视觉数据是被学得并被诠释的，因此它们显得好像是那些数据唯一可能的结果。内在视像能令你惶惑，因为在你的心智中，你常很清楚的看见那些如果你的眼镜睁开时，你将拒斥的形象。不过，以我们现在的说话方式，年轻期的人类对我称之为「内在感官」的使用比你们要多得多。视觉上，早期人类看物理世界与你们看来好像很自然的世界是不一样的。", "en": "Whatever your language, you perceive trees, mountains, people, oceans. You never see a man merge with a tree, for example. This would be considered an hallucinatory image. Your visual data are learned and interpreted so that they appear as the only possible results of those data. Inner vision can confound you, because in your mind you often see images quite clearly that you would dismiss if your eyes were open. In the terms of which we are speaking, however, the young species utilized what I have called the “inner senses” to a far greater degree than you do. Visually, early man did not perceive the physical world in the way that seems natural to you.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第777节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "777", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 58}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 16}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 10}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 6}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 4}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 4}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 1}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 1}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1979], "stats": {"blocks": 11, "quotes": 113, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 1, "only_en": 2}};
